3	Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek	deluxe-annapurna-circuit-trek	15 Days Guided Himalayan Adventure	deluxe-trekking	Annapurna	deluxe-nepal-trekking-tours	15	1899	2300	1999	2400	Moderate	5,416m (Thorong La) / 4,130m (ABC)	Spring (Mar-May) & Autumn (Sep-Nov)	4-Star City Hotel & Deluxe Attached-Bath Lodges	Full Board (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) on Trek	2 – 12 Guests (Private or Small Group)	t	bestseller	/images/upload/package/deluxe-annapurna-circuit-trek.jpg	["/images/upload/package/slider/deluxe-annapurna-circuit-trek.jpg"]	<h1>Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek &ndash; 15 Days</h1>\r\n\r\n<p><em>One of the Most Popular Trekking Adventures in Nepal&rsquo;s Annapurna Region</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>The <strong>Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek &ndash; 15 Days</strong> is one of Nepal&rsquo;s most rewarding trekking adventures, combining the spectacular Tilicho Lake (4,919 m), the sacred Muktinath Temple, and the breathtaking crossing of Thorong La Pass (5,416 m). The journey also includes scenic hikes around Ngawal and Manang villages, both situated above 3,500 m, offering spectacular mountain views and unforgettable Himalayan landscapes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Along the way, you can enjoy natural hot springs, traditional villages, local culture, and visits to two of Nepal&rsquo;s most popular tourist cities, Kathmandu and Pokhara. One of the most appealing features of the Annapurna Circuit Trek is that the route begins and ends in different locations, allowing you to experience changing landscapes and new scenery throughout the journey.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>What Is the Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek, and What Makes It Deluxe?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The <strong>Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek</strong> offers an upgraded trekking experience with carefully selected lodges featuring attached bathrooms where available, private transportation for road journeys, and quality meals throughout the trek. These added comforts make the journey more convenient while allowing you to enjoy the natural beauty and cultural highlights of the Annapurna region.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The Annapurna Circuit is widely recognized as one of the world&rsquo;s great long-distance trekking routes. Besisahar (760 m) is the traditional starting point of the journey, while motor roads now connect several sections of the Manang Valley. From Kathmandu, we travel by road toward Chame (2,700 m), with the journey arranged over two days. From Chame, the trekking adventure begins, gradually ascending through Lower and Upper Pisang toward Manang.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The itinerary includes time to acclimatize in the high-altitude Manang region before continuing toward Yak Kharka and Thorong Phedi. The highest point of the trek is <strong>Thorong La Pass (5,416 m)</strong>, one of the most memorable highlights of the Annapurna Circuit. After crossing the pass, the route descends into the Lower Mustang region, where you visit the sacred Muktinath Temple, a place of great religious significance to both Hindus and Buddhists.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>After Muktinath, the journey continues through the Mustang region toward Tatopani, whose name means &ldquo;hot water&rdquo; in Nepali. Here, you can relax in natural hot springs before continuing toward the final trekking destinations. The extended route through Ghorepani and Poon Hill, followed by Ghandruk village, offers additional opportunities to enjoy Himalayan scenery and traditional mountain culture before reaching the Pokhara area.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>One of the key advantages of this deluxe trekking package is the variety of landscapes and settlements along the route. Because the Annapurna Circuit is connected by motor roads at several points, we use transportation where planned at the beginning, middle, and end of the journey. This helps reduce unnecessary walking along road sections while preserving the major trekking highlights. Carefully selected deluxe lodges and quality meals further enhance comfort throughout the adventure.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Why Should You Book a Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek With Us?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Here are some reasons to choose our Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek in Nepal:</p>\r\n\r\n<ol start="1">\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Enjoy upgraded lodge accommodation and hygienic meals throughout the trek.</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Trek with professional Expert Representatives and porters.</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Follow a carefully planned itinerary designed with safety, acclimatization, and comfort in mind.</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p>Experience an upgraded trekking package with selected accommodations and transportation arrangements for a more comfortable journey.</p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<h2>Is the Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek Suitable for Me? How Difficult Is It?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The highest point of the Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek is <strong>Thorong La Pass at 5,416 m (17,764 ft)</strong>. Since the route involves trekking at high altitudes and crossing a mountain pass above 5,000 m, it is generally considered a <strong>moderately difficult to challenging trek</strong>.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you have approximately two weeks available and enjoy trekking through forested trails, alpine landscapes, high mountain valleys, and traditional villages, this adventure may be an excellent choice. Along the way, you will experience a combination of high-altitude trekking, sacred temples, natural hot springs, local culture, and spectacular Himalayan mountain scenery.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Previous trekking experience, good physical fitness, proper acclimatization, and a suitable pace are important for completing the journey safely.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Best Season for the Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>The best time for the Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek depends on the mountain views, weather conditions, and landscapes you wish to experience.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Autumn (October to mid-December):</strong> Autumn is one of the best seasons for trekking in the Annapurna region. The weather is often clear, offering excellent opportunities to enjoy crystal-clear mountain views and spectacular Himalayan scenery.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Spring (March to May):</strong> Spring is another excellent season for the Annapurna Circuit Trek. The weather becomes warmer, and blooming wildflowers add color to the trekking trails and mountain landscapes.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Although the Annapurna Circuit can be trekked during other months, <strong>January and February are generally less favorable</strong> because of extreme cold, snowfall, and possible difficulties crossing Thorong La Pass. Winter conditions can affect route safety and accessibility, so seasonal weather and trail conditions should always be checked before departure.</p>	Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek - 15 Days One of the Most Popular Trekking Adventures in Nepal's Annapurna Region The Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek - 15 Days is one of Nepal's most rewarding trekking adventures, combining the spectacular Tilicho Lake (4,919 m), the sacred Muktinath Temple, and the breathtaking crossing of Thorong La Pass (5,416 m). The journey also includes scenic hikes around Ngawal and Manang villages, both situated above 3,500 m, offering spectacular mountain views and unforgettable Himalayan landscapes. Along the way, you can enjoy natural hot springs, traditional villages, local culture, and visits to two of Nepal's most popular tourist cities, Kathmandu and Pokhara. One of the most appealing features of the Annapurna Circuit Trek is that the route begins and ends in different locations, allowing you to experience changing landscapes and new scenery throughout the journey. What Is the Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek, and What Makes It Deluxe? The Deluxe Annapurna Circuit Trek offers an upgraded trekking experience with carefully selected lodges featuring attached bathrooms where available, private transportation for road journeys, and quality meals throughout the 	<ul>\r\n\t<li>An iconic trek to Tilicho Lake (4,919 m), a stunning high-altitude lake surrounded by mountains with crystal-clear water.</li>\r\n\t<li>One of the world&rsquo;s best trekking routes.</li>\r\n\t<li>A moderate-to-difficult trek that includes crossing Thorong La Pass (5,416 m).</li>\r\n\t<li>Enjoy different landscapes and mountain views every day as the trail begins and ends in different locations.</li>\r\n\t<li>Drive along road sections to reduce walking time, noise, and discomfort during the Annapurna Circuit Trek.</li>\r\n\t<li>Visit the holy temple of Muktinath.</li>\r\n\t<li>Bathe in the natural hot springs of Tatopani.</li>\r\n\t<li>Enjoy cultural sightseeing in Pokhara.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div>\r\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>	<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif"><strong>Comfortable, deluxe accommodations and hygienic meals</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 4&nbsp;or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in&nbsp;<span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>KATHMANDU&nbsp;o</strong></span>n twin share with breakfast&nbsp;<span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)">(2<strong>&nbsp;nights)</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 4&nbsp;or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in&nbsp;<span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>POKHARA</strong></span>&nbsp;on twin share with breakfast&nbsp;<span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)">(<strong>1&nbsp;nights)</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><strong>8 nights at a deluxe mountain lodge&nbsp;</strong></span>or guest house with an attached bathroom, including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>3 nights at the best selected lodge</strong></span>&nbsp;or guest house with a common bathroom including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">There are 3 hygienic vegetarian or non-vegetarian meals per day: breakfast, lunch, and dinner (you can choose meals from all over the Lodge every day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tea/coffee or other hot beverages during breakfast, lunch, and dinner (5&ndash;6 cups per day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">seasonal fruits and additional biscuit/cookies snacks&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Private transportation that is comfortable</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">private, comfortable vehicle tour of Pokhara City&nbsp;as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">All airport transfers by private, comfortable vehicle (international and domestic airport pick-up and drop-off as included in the itinerary).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:#800000">Kathmandu- Besis</span><span style="color:#8B4513">ahar by Private comfortable car( starting day of trek)</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="color:#8B4513"><span style="font-size:16px">Besisahar- chame by Private&nbsp;Jeep</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="color:#8B4513"><span style="font-size:16px">Muktinath- Pokhara&nbsp;by Private Jeep</span></span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>baggage allowance and domestic flights.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="color:#8B4513"><strong><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-size:16px">Pokhara-Kathmandu flight tickets</span></span></strong></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-size:16px">The baggage allowance on the Pokhara&nbsp;flight is 15 kg, and we include 5 kg extra for free, for a total of 20 kg per person</span>.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Professional Private Expert Representatives &amp; porters</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">professional English-speaking tour guide for sightseeing in the city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A professional English-speaking guide for the trek</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Porter who is professional, dependable, helpful, and friendly (1 porter for every two people sharing)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Daily wage, lodging, meals, and guide and porter insurance.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Trekking permits and entrance fees</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Entrance fees to all UNESCO heritage sites during city sightseeing in&nbsp; Pokhara</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Annapurna conservation Area Project( ACAP)&nbsp;Entrance&nbsp;Fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The local government fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekker&rsquo;s information management system (TIMS) fee</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free information or guest services.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">guide to purchasing trekking clothing or equipment, as well as any other required wholesale shopping in Kathmandu.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support in the case of baggage loss or delay in Kathmandu from international flights to Nepal</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support to exchange money, get a local SIM card</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">24/7 emergency call support.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free safe baggage storage service during the trek</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free welcome dinner &amp; farewell professional body massage after the trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">We offer a free welcome Nepalese dinner with authentic Nepalese cultural dances on arrival day, or if you arrive late on arrival night, this will be provided on the second day.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">After the trek, you will receive a FREE 1-hour Ayurvedic full-body massage as a treatment for your tired body.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Other free services include:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A down sleeping bag and a down jacket are provided at no cost.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of water bottles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of trekking poles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of porter duffel bags (you can take them after the trek if you like).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">First Aid Kit</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking certificate</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking Map</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The company&#39;s gift</span></li>\r\n</ul>	<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Nepal Visa-US $ 50</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">International Flight to/from Kathmandu/home</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Travel and Emergency Helicopter Evacuation Insurance</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Meals (Lunch and Dinner) and other expenses while in Kathmandu 