1	Deluxe Everest Base Camp Trek	deluxe-everest-base-camp-trek	High Quality, all-inclusive trek staying at exclusive Deluxe Lodges in Mountain	deluxe-trekking	Everest	deluxe-nepal-trekking-tours	14	1899	2200	1999	2300	Moderate	5,545m (Kala Patthar)	Spring (Mar-May) & Autumn (Sep-Nov)	4-Star City Hotel & Deluxe Attached-Bath Lodges	Full Board (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) on Trek	2 – 12 Guests (Private or Small Group)	t	bestseller	/images/upload/package/deluxe-everest-base-camp-trek.jpg	["/images/upload/package/slider/deluxe-everest-base-camp-trek-1.jpg", "/images/upload/package/slider/deluxe-everest-base-camp-trek-1-1.jpg"]	<p><span style="font-size:22px"><strong>Deluxe&nbsp;Everest Base Camp trek-14&nbsp;days</strong></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="142"><span style="font-size:18px"><em>exclusive mountain Deluxe Lodges on a high-quality, all-inclusive trek</em></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>What is the Deluxe Everest Base Camp Trek and what makes it Deluxe?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p data-end="525" data-start="121"><span style="font-size:16px">Situated at an altitude of 5,364m, the base camp of Everest is the highest point on earth, and the Deluxe Everest Base Camp Trek is one of the most popular and highly recommended luxury-style treks in Nepal. This trek is one of the shortest-duration treks to reach the base camp of Mount Everest. Flying in and out of Lukla is the shortest and most convenient way to start and end this world-famous trek.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p data-end="832" data-start="527"><span style="font-size:16px">Some of the main highlights of the Everest trek include the spectacular Himalayan ranges, Tengboche Monastery, and Kala Patthar. Hiking and trekking to the highest points in the Himalayas&mdash;especially reaching the base camps of Mount Everest and Kala Patthar&mdash;is a dream trip of a lifetime for all travelers.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p data-end="1213" data-start="834"><span style="font-size:16px">This outstanding adventure trek begins after two days of historical sightseeing in Kathmandu and allows time to adjust to jet lag, especially for travelers coming from long distances such as the USA or Canada. Our Everest Base Camp Trek starts with a 35-minute scenic mountain flight to Lukla, one of the busiest small airports serving all Everest treks and climbing expeditions.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p data-end="1721" data-start="1215"><span style="font-size:16px">We continue towards Namche Bazaar, a Sherpa settlement at an altitude of 3,440m, where we spend two days for the first acclimatization. From Namche, the trek proceeds with a visit to the famous Tengboche Monastery, which offers the best views of the magnificent Ama Dablam mountain. We spend one night there before continuing to Pheriche for two days. At an altitude of 4,400m, we begin acclimatization and hike to the highest point of Nagarjun to keep ourselves fit and well-adjusted to the high altitude.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p data-end="2026" data-start="1723"><span style="font-size:16px">After two more days of trekking, we finally reach our dream destination&mdash;Everest Base Camp at 5,364m. The next morning, at sunrise, we hike to the highest point of this trek, Kala Patthar, at 5,644m. The main aim of this Deluxe Everest Base Camp Trek is to reach both Everest Base Camp and Kala Patthar.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p data-end="2428" data-start="2028"><span style="font-size:16px">After completing the trek, we follow the same route back to Lukla and fly to Kathmandu. This entire Everest Base Camp Trek follows a well-crafted 16-day itinerary by Nepal Trekking Tourism &amp; Adventure, offering the most comfortable deluxe hotels and lodges throughout the trek. To ensure a premium experience, we have selected the best available lodges to provide deluxe services and maximum comfort.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p data-end="2428" data-start="2028"><span style="font-size:16px">This Everest Base Camp Deluxe Trek is one of the all-inclusive trek packages for a comfortable and most enjoyable dream holiday for all trekkers from around the world. However, if you would like to have the best upgraded version of the Everest Base Camp Kala Patthar trek package, you can also consider our <a href="https://www.nepaltrekkingtours.com/luxury-everest-base-camp-trek">14-day Luxury Everest Base Camp Trek</a> for a truly amazing luxury experience and the best adventure of your life.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Why should you book a Deluxe Everest Base Camp Trek with us?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="149"><span style="font-size:16px">The deluxe trek to Everest Base Camp is an upgraded trekking package of CCC Nepal trekking tours. When compared to the over 1000 Everest base camp packages available, this type of deluxe package provides the highest quality lodge accommodation on the trek. We offer not only the best lodge accommodation, but we have also upgraded the quality of personalized service from our professional guides for safety and comfort. Here are four reasons to book the deluxe EBC trek only with us.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="150"><span style="font-size:16px">In order to experience the highest level of comfort by staying at deluxe lodges in Trek with hot shower facilities,</span></li>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="150"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-size:16px">A well-planned itinerary for a safe and enjoyable trek</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="150"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-size:16px">A professional Expert Representative with experience of over 15 years plus</span></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="150"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-size:16px">quality of self-selected meals every day in deluxe lodges.</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Is this trek for me? How difficult is this trek?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="155"><span style="font-size:16px">This is a moderate-level 11-day trek. You don&rsquo;t have to be athletic or a player to complete this trek. You just need to be physically fit and mentally prepared to walk 5-7 hours per day for this trek. For best acclimatization, there are two acclimatization days at 3400m and 4400m.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>The best season for the Deluxe Everest Base Camp Trek:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="157"><span style="font-size:16px">The best weather months for all Everest treks are mid-September to mid-December and March to May. However, this trek is possible in other months too. January and February are the coldest winter months, and mid-June to mid-September is the monsoon season, so weather is not favorable for this trek.</span></p>	Deluxe Everest Base Camp trek-14 days exclusive mountain Deluxe Lodges on a high-quality, all-inclusive trek What is the Deluxe Everest Base Camp Trek and what makes it Deluxe? Situated at an altitude of 5,364m, the base camp of Everest is the highest point on earth, and the Deluxe Everest Base Camp Trek is one of the most popular and highly recommended luxury-style treks in Nepal. This trek is one of the shortest-duration treks to reach the base camp of Mount Everest. Flying in and out of Lukla is the shortest and most convenient way to start and end this world-famous trek. Some of the main highlights of the Everest trek include the spectacular Himalayan ranges, Tengboche Monastery, and Kala Patthar. Hiking and trekking to the highest points in the Himalayas-especially reaching the base camps of Mount Everest and Kala Patthar-is a dream trip of a lifetime for all travelers. This outstanding adventure trek begins after two days of historical sightseeing in Kathmandu and allows time to adjust to jet lag, especially for travelers coming from long distances such as the USA or Canada. Our Everest Base Camp Trek starts with a 35-minute scenic mountain flight to Lukla, one of the busiest	<ol>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">The best, highly recommended, most popular trekking in the world.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Trek that is well-prepared, valuable, and a once-in-a-lifetime experience.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Hike to Everest base camp( 5364m)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Sunrise hike to Kalapatthar(5640m)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Sleep in the best mountain lodges available.</span></li>\r\n</ol>	<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#8B4513"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif"><strong>Comfortable, deluxe accommodations and hygienic meals</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 4&nbsp;or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in Kathmandu on twin share with breakfast (2&nbsp;nights).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">7 nights at a deluxe mountain lodge or guest house with an attached bathroom, including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">4 nights at the best selected lodge or guest house with a common bathroom including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">There are 3 hygienic vegetarian or non-vegetarian meals per day: breakfast, lunch, and dinner (you can choose meals from all over the Lodge every day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tea/coffee or other hot beverages during breakfast, lunch, and dinner (5&ndash;6 cups per day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">seasonal fruits and additional biscuit/cookies snacks&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#8B4513"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Private transportation that is comfortable</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">private, comfortable vehicle tour of Kathmandu city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">All airport transfers by private, comfortable vehicle (international and domestic airport pick-up and drop-off as included in the itinerary).</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#8B4513"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>baggage allowance and domestic flights.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:14px">K<span style="font-size:16px">athmandu-Lukla-Kathmandu flight tickets</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-size:16px">The baggage allowance on the Lukla flight is 15 kg, and we include 5 kg extra for free, for a total of 20 kg per person</span>.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#8B4513"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Professional Private Expert Representatives &amp; porters</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A professional English-speaking guide for the trek</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Porter who is professional, dependable, helpful, and friendly (1 porter for every two people sharing)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Daily wage, lodging, meals, and guide and porter insurance.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#8B4513"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Trekking permits and entrance fees</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Everest National Park Fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The local government fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekker&rsquo;s information management system (TIMS) fee</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#8B4513"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free information or guest services.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">guide to purchasing trekking clothing or equipment, as well as any other required wholesale shopping in Kathmandu.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support in the case of baggage loss or delay in Kathmandu from international flights to Nepal</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support to exchange money, get a local SIM card</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">24/7 emergency call support.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free safe baggage storage service during the trek</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#8B4513"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free welcome dinner &amp; farewell professional body massage after the trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">We offer a free welcome Nepalese dinner with authentic Nepalese cultural dances on arrival day, or if you arrive late on arrival night, this will be provided on the second day.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">After the trek, you will receive a FREE 1-hour Ayurvedic full-body massage as a treatment for your tired body.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#8B4513"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Other free services include:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A down sleeping bag and a down jacket are provided at no cost.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of water bottles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of trekking poles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of porter duffel bags (you can take them after the trek if you like).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">First Aid Kit</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking certificate</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking Map</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The company&#39;s gift</span></li>\r\n</ul>	<ul style="color: #252525;">\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Nepal Visa-US $ 50</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">International Flight to/from Kathmandu/home</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Travel and Emergency Helicopter Evacuation Insurance</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Meals (Lunch and Dinner) and other expenses while in Kathmandu (breakfast included at hotel)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Any soft drinks or alcoholic drinks during the trek, drinking water, battery charges, internet bills, dessert items, Except for breakfast, lunch, and dinner, extra tea/coffee or foods</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Laundry or personal expenses like internet WIFI, unforeseen costs due to natural disasters, sickness, flight delays, bad weather, urgent helicopter evacuation etc.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking gear and clothing</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tips for guides and porters</span></li>\r\n</ul>	<p>Notes</p>	[{"label": "1 Traveler (Solo Private)", "maxPax": 1, "minPax": 1, "deluxePrice": 2149, "luxuryPrice": 2349}, {"label": "2 – 3 Travelers", "maxPax": 3, "minPax": 2, "deluxePrice": 1899, "luxuryPrice": 1999}, {"label": "4 – 6 Travelers", "maxPax": 6, "minPax": 4, "deluxePrice": 1766, "luxuryPrice": 1859}, {"label": "7 – 12 Travelers (Group)", "maxP