"15km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "The Edelweiss Lodge or Similar (B/L/D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 11, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B/L/D)", "title": "Day 11: Trek return back to Namche (3440M), second Last day trek of Luxury EBC trek -  8/9 hrs- MLN(B/L/D)", "walking": "8-9 hours Trekking", "altitude": "3440m", "distance": "14.2 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "MLN(B/L/D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 12, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B/L/D)", "title": "Day 12: Trek return back to Lukla, last day trek of EBC Luxury trek- 7/8 hrs- MLN( B+ L+D)", "walking": "7-8 hours trekking", "altitude": "2860m", "distance": "13.5 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "MLN( B+ L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 13, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Day 13: Lukla to Kathmandu by Flight( 35 min), Transfer to hotel & relax day at Hotel- Hotel Marriot( B/B)", "walking": "-", "altitude": "1400m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Hotel Marriot( B+ B))- 5 * Luxury in Kathmandu", "transportation": "Flights + Private car transfer"}, {"day": 14, "meal": "Lavish Breakfast", "title": "Day 14: Your Luxury Everest base camp trek ends today, drive to Airport & Fly to home. SEE YOU AGAIN- B", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "-", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "-", "transportation": "Private Car to Airport"}]	[{"id": 51, "price": 3300, "status": "Guaranteed", "endDate": "2026-11-15", "spotsLeft": 6, "startDate": "2026-11-01"}, {"id": 52, "price": 3300, "status": "Available", "endDate": "2026-11-29", "spotsLeft": 8, "startDate": "2026-11-15"}, {"id": 53, "price": 3300, "status": "Available", "endDate": "2026-12-19", "spotsLeft": 10, "startDate": "2026-12-05"}, {"id": 54, "price": 3300, "status": "Available", "endDate": "2027-03-24", "spotsLeft": 12, "startDate": "2027-03-10"}, {"id": 55, "price": 3300, "status": "Guaranteed", "endDate": "2027-04-16", "spotsLeft": 5, "startDate": "2027-04-02"}]	[]	[{"id": 3, "date": "2022-07-22", "title": "Amanda", "author": "Luxury Everest base camp trek", "rating": 5, "comment": "We found Expert Representative's company very professional in quick response. All the service from beginning to end was fabulous. We had a great trek in Nepal. Our guide was Lhakpa Sherpa and a very nice guide throughout the trip to Everest base camp. We enjoyed the all-luxury hotels and lodges. A very well-organized trek. we are going to use Nepal trekking company again for another trip soon. Amanda,", "country": "Australia"}, {"id": 53, "date": "2025-04-20", "title": "Riccardo", "author": "Highly Recommended Luxury Everest Trek", "rating": 5, "comment": "I highly recommend this trek to anyone looking for a comfortable lodge experience in the Everest region, even if it means paying a bit more - it's absolutely worth it! My wife and I had a wonderful trekking experience in Everest in October 2024, thanks to Expert Representative's well-crafted itinerary, which worked perfectly for us. The lodges we stayed in were very comfortable, with hot showers in the rooms almost everywhere, except in Lobuche and Gorakshep, where facilities are naturally more basic due to the high altitude. We stayed at the Hotel Dwarika in Kathmandu, which was a true 5-star luxury experience. Along the trail, the MLN lodges in Lukla and Namche were excellent, and even the lodges up to Dingboche were among the best available at that altitude - clean, warm, and welcoming.Our guide Tandi was fantastic - knowledgeable, friendly, and very attentive throughout the trek. Our porter Sangey, a kind and strong Sherpa, was also wonderful and made our journey much easier. NETTA is a true Sherpa company in Nepal with over 25 years of trekking experience, and their upgraded luxury trekking service is something I would recommend to everyone. We had no issues at all with hot water, showers, meals, or accommodations. Everything was well arranged, and we were always well-fed and well taken care of. Thank you to Expert Representative and the entire NETTA team for this unforgettable experience in Nepal! - Riccardo, Isreal", "country": "Isreal"}, {"id": 54, "date": "2025-04-20", "title": "Dave", "author": "An Unforgettable Trekking Experience with NETTA", "rating": 5, "comment": "My wife and I recently had an incredible trekking experience in Nepal, organized by NETTA (Nepal Trekking & Tourism & Adventure). From start to finish, everything was handled with professionalism and care. Our guide, Tashi Tamang , was exceptionally polite, helpful, and attentive throughout the entire trek. His warm demeanor and deep knowledge of the region made the journey both enjoyable and informative. Our porter, Sangey , was equally impressive - a kind and dedicated individual who ensured our comfort and safety every step of the way. The lodges along the trekking route were clean, cozy, and comfortable, offering a much-needed rest after long days on the trail. The food was consistently delicious and exceeded our expectations. Additionally, the hotel in Kathmandu was top-class - truly among the best in Nepal. Overall, this was a memorable and enriching trekking experience that we will cherish for years to come. We wholeheartedly recommend NETTA to anyone planning a trek in Nepal. You'll be in excellent hands with Expert Representative and his outstanding team. Best regards, Dave, Canada", "country": "canada"}, {"id": 55, "date": "2025-04-20", "title": "Craig", "author": "Exceptional Luxury Trekking Experience in Everest base camp", "rating": 5, "comment": "NETTA organizes a truly outstanding luxury trekking experience in Nepal. I had previously trekked in Nepal with another company a few years ago, but this time with NETTA, the difference was clear - their quality, attention to detail, and level of service are simply unmatched. From beginning to end, the trek was smooth, comfortable, and incredibly well-organized. The luxury lodges we stayed in during the trek were the best available - clean, cozy, and offering stunning views. In Kathmandu, we stayed at a 5-star hotel that delivered first-class comfort and service. The meals throughout the journey were delicious and of top quality, and we never had to worry about drinking water or hot beverages - everything was taken care of. The trekking staff were phenomenal - highly professional, friendly, and genuinely caring. Their support made the entire experience feel effortless and enjoyable. I'm already looking forward to coming back for another luxury trek in the Annapurna region with NETTA in the near future. Sincerely, Craig, USA", "country": "usa"}, {"id": 56, "date": "2025-04-20", "title": "Stephen", "author": "Incredible 15-Day Luxury Everest Base Camp Trek", "rating": 5, "comment": "I recently completed a 15-day Luxury Everest Base Camp Trek with Expert Representative's company, and I can confidently say it was an unforgettable experience from start to finish. From the moment I arrived in Kathmandu, everything was perfectly organized - from the warm welcome at the airport to the lovely welcome dinner and, of course, the entire trek itself. My guide, Mingmar Sherpa, and my porter, Harka Rai, were both outstanding - professional, kind, and incredibly supportive throughout the journey. What truly sets this trek apart is the quality of the accommodations. The lodges booked for us in the mountains were the best available, offering comfort, warmth, and excellent service even at high altitudes. The luxury package provided by NETTA is, without a doubt, the best I've come across. Every detail was thoughtfully arranged - including great meals, reliable drinking water, and hot beverages along the way. The hotel in Kathmandu was top-class and a perfect place to relax before and after the trek. A heartfelt thank you to Expert Representative for organizing such a well-run and memorable trek. I'm already looking forward to joining another trek with NETTA and highly recommend this experience to anyone considering trekking in Nepal. Stephen, UK", "country": "UK"}]	5.0	13	2026-10-23 20:31:04.764319+06
24	Deluxe Mera Peak Expedition	deluxe-mera-peak-expedition	17 Days Guided Himalayan Adventure	peak-climbing	Everest / Khumbu	peak-climbing-in-nepal	17	2599	2900	2699	3000	Challenging / Expedition	6,476m / 21,246ft	Spring (Mar-May) & Autumn (Sep-Nov)	4-Star City Hotel & Deluxe Attached-Bath Lodges	Full Board (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) on Trek	2 – 12 Guests (Private or Small Group)	t	peak	/images/upload/package/deluxe-mera-peak-expedition.jpg	["/images/upload/package/slider/deluxe-mera-peak-expedition.jpg"]	<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="519"><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Deluxe Mera Peak Expedition-17&nbsp;days</strong></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="true" data-paragraphid="520"><span style="font-size:16px"><em>&quot;One of the highest, non-technical, best-view trekking peaks in Nepal for an experience of a lifetime with the best itinerary&quot;</em></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="true" data-paragraphid="520"><span style="color:#008080"><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Deluxe Mera Peak Expedition Cost &ndash; 17-Day Full-Board Package</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul data-spread="false">\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="color:#008080"><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Autumn Price (Mid-September to Mid-December):</strong> USD 2,599 per person.</span></span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="color:#008080"><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Spring Price (March to May):</strong> USD 2,777 per person.</span></span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="521"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><strong>What is the Deluxe Mera&nbsp;Peak Expedition &amp; what makes it Deluxe?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="522"><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>The Deluxe Mera Peak Expedition</strong>&nbsp;is a premier trekking and&nbsp;climbing adventure trip in the Everest region of Nepal. Mera peak is said to be one of the highest trekking peaks, situated at an altitude of 6476m. Technically less difficult than other trekking peaks, this peak is a very popular trekking peak in Nepal. NETTA is a 25-year old expert local Sherpa trekking and mountaineering agency based in Kathmandu that offers a 21-day fully guided special cost package for Mera peak climbing. Even though Mera peak is not harder to summit or even if trekking is not much harder to reach, the views from the top of Mera peak are unforgettable. Once you are at the top of Mera peak (6476m), you will be mesmerized by the mesmerizing panoramic Himalayan views of Mount Everest, Kanchenjunga, Lhotse, Makalu, Cho Oyu and other grand peaks of the Himalaya.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="523"><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking and peak climbing like Mera Peak, which is an adventure trekking and climbing journey of a lifetime, starts and ends in Kathmandu. After two days of jet lag or cultural city sightseeing or trip preparation, you will take a 35-minute mountain flight to Lukla Airport, which is known as the Gateway to Mount Everest and other Himalayan peaks for trekking and climbing. From Lukla, there are two trails to trek toward Mera peak. Our package itinerary slowly starts through the less crowded trail of Panggom, the local Sherpa village. Before heading to the summit, we will already have acclimatized well to adjust to high altitude sickness. We have set up two full days of acclimatization at Thangnak and Khare before we push to the summit of Mera Peak. Please remember that two days in Thangnak and two days in Khare are very important acclimatization days and don&rsquo;t avoid them.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="524"><span style="font-size:16px">Leaving the Khare, our Mera peak itinerary follows one overnight stay at Mera base camp and another overnight stay at High camp. Technically, Mera peak is said to be not that hard to climb. However, the route to reach Mera peak is longer than other trekking peaks of the Everest region. After a successful summit of Mera peak, you will return back to Khare and follow the trailhead to Lukla via a shorter way. The lodges or guest houses on the Mera Peak route are not as luxurious as those on the regular Everest base camp route, but we will accommodate you at the best available lodges or guest houses with hot showers or attached bathrooms, so this excellent climbing expedition is known as the Deluxe Mera Peak expedition.This is excellent and high-class oriented trekking and peak climbing in Nepal with us.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="525"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><strong>Why should you book the Deluxe Mera peak expedition with us?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="530"><span style="font-size:16px"><em>Here are five reasons to book your mera peak with us in Nepal.</em></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="531">\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px">First of all, the Deluxe Mera Peak is a well-crafted package with enough acclimatization days for a safe and comfortable peak climbing experience.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="531">\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px">We offer over 15 years of expert sherpa guidance for a 100% successful ascent of Mera Peak.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="531">\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px">We provide the best available lodges with hygenic meals, safe and comfortable trekking and climbing.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="531">\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px">The best value for money.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="531">\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px">The highest quality of accommodation, transportation, and personalized service throughout the entire trip.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="526"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><strong>Is this trekking and climbing for me? How difficult is the Mera peak climbing expedition?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="527"><span style="font-size:16px">Mera peak expedition, like other peaks, requires physical fitness and basic climbing experience; however, because Mera peak is a less technical peak to summit, if you have previous experience trekking at an altitude of around or above 4000 m, you can easily climb this peak.The daily trekking hours are from 6&ndash;9 hrs. Once you have booked the trip with us, we advise you to start running, walking, or hiking in the hills or in the park. A daily minimum of 1-2 hrs. of cycling, jogging, or running can help a lot on this trip.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="528"><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><strong>The best season for the Deluxe Mera Peak Expedition:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="529"><span style="font-size:16px">Like all other treks and climbing trips, the best time to trek and summit Mera peak is mid-September to mid-December, but the best core months in the fall season are mid-October to early December. In spring, the best months are April and May. June is early monsoon season and still okay to summit a peak. March is a nice spring month to climb Mera peak.</span></p>	Deluxe Mera Peak Expedition-17 days "One of the highest, non-technical, best-view trekking peaks in Nepal for an experience of a lifetime with the best itinerary" Deluxe Mera Peak Expedition Cost - 17-Day Full-Board Package Autumn Price (Mid-September to Mid-December): USD 2,599 per person. Spring Price (March to May): USD 2,777 per person. What is the Deluxe Mera Peak Expedition & what makes it Deluxe? The Deluxe Mera Peak Expedition is a premier trekking and climbing adventure trip in the Everest region of Nepal. Mera peak is said to be one of the highest trekking peaks, situated at an altitude of 6476m. Technically less difficult than other trekking peaks, this peak is a very popular trekking peak in Nepal. NETTA is a 25-year old expert local Sherpa trekking and mountaineering agency based in Kathmandu that offers a 21-day fully guided special cost package for Mera peak climbing. Even though Mera peak is not harder to summit or even if trekking is not much harder to reach, the views from the top of Mera peak are unforgettable. Once you are at the top of Mera peak (6476m), you will be mesmerized by the mesmerizing panoramic Himalayan views of Mount Everest, Kanchenjunga, Lhotse, 	<ol>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Mera Peak is the highest non-technical trekking and climbing package in Nepal.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Experience the most valuable, well-crafted itinerary that offers 100 % safe acclimatization for a 100 % successful summit.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">You will stay at the best available selected lodge or guest house throughout the trek with a hot shower.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Two nights at comfortable tented camps with the best possible service to summit Mera peak.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Trekking through the lower beautiful route of Panggom to see more spectacular views</span></li>\r\n</ol>	<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif"><strong>Comfortable, deluxe accommodations and hygienic meals</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 4&nbsp;or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in Kathmandu on twin share with breakfast&nbsp;<span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>(2&nbsp;nights).</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>13&nbsp;nights at the best selected lodge or guest house</strong></span>&nbsp;with a common bathroom including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>1 nights at Tented camp&nbsp;</strong></span>during climbing of MERA&nbsp;peak</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">There are 3 hygienic vegetarian or non-vegetarian meals per day: breakfast, lunch, and dinner (you can choose meals from all over the Lodge every day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tea/coffee or other hot beverages during breakfast, lunch, and dinner (5&ndash;6 cups per day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">seasonal fruits and additional biscuit/cookies snacks&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Private transportation that is comfortable</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">All airport transfers by private, comfortable vehicle (international and domestic airport pick-up and drop-off as included in the itinerary).</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>baggage allowance and domestic flights.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="color:rgb(128, 