t Khare to Mera high camp( 5800m), overnight at Tented camp( B+L+D)- 5-7 hours hike today>>Tented camp( B+L+D)", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "5800 m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Tented camp( B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 12, "meal": "Breakfast + lunch + Dinner(B/L/D)", "title": "Day 13: trek back to Kothe>> 5-6 hours>>  Best available lodge( B+L+D)", "walking": "5-6 hours of trekking", "altitude": "3580 m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Best available lodge( B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 13, "meal": "Breakfast + lunch + Dinner(B/L/D)", "title": "Day 14: Trek back to Thuli Kharka/ Chhertrabuk>> 5-7 hours- Best available lodge( B+L+D)", "walking": "5-7 hours of trekking", "altitude": "4200m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Best available lodge( B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 14, "meal": "Breakfast + lunch + Dinner(B/L/D)", "title": "Day 15: Trek back to Lukla>> Deluxe attached bathroom lodge( B+L+D)", "walking": "6-8 hours trekking", "altitude": "2860 m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe attached bathroom lodge( B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 15, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Day 16: Lukla to Kathmandu flight, transfer to hotel, free day to relax or shopping etc- Deluxe hotel( B+B)", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "1400 m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe hotel( B+B)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 16, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Day 17: drive to Airport and fly home... mera peak expedition ends here.. see you again.", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "1400m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe Attached-Bath Lodge", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}]	[{"id": 245, "price": 2599, "status": 1, "endDate": "2026-12-01", "spotsLeft": 5, "startDate": "2026-11-15"}, {"id": 246, "price": 2599, "status": 1, "endDate": "2026-12-16", "spotsLeft": 7, "startDate": "2026-11-30"}]	[]	[{"id": 23, "date": "2022-07-27", "title": " David Hams", "author": "Deluxe Mera Peak Expedition", "rating": 5, "comment": "For many years, I have dreamt of trekking and climbing low-altitude mountains in Nepal. When I was researching trekking and climbing small mountains, I came across a CCC Nepal trekking tours company that offers a special deluxe trekking and climbing trip in Nepal. I found their deluxe package of Mera peak climbing very attractive and worthwhile. So I have booked this expedition with Mr. Expert Representative in November 2022. Expert Representative is very quick to respond and so helpful in planning this expedition with very proper information. So we two (my wife and I) booked the Mera Peak expedition with CCC Nepal Trekking Tours. We were overjoyed to be in Nepal, and when he greeted us at Kathmandu Airport in the traditional Sherpa manner, we were overjoyed. were also offered a free welcome dinner, which was a great first day in Kathmandu. On the trek, we had a very friendly and honest guide who always made sure that we were enjoying the trek. The lodges in this area do not have much higher standards, but our guide booked us in the cleanest and best available lodges every night. The most important thing is the itinerary. The itinerary set up on their website is a very well planned one. It is a very nice itinerary for acclimatization and safety purposes. We have finally reached the top of Mera peak, and the weather was perfect on the climbing day. The views from the top of Mera Peak were just amazing. Our porter and guide are so helpful for this trip. Without them, this trip couldn't be successful. All other services, such as a hotel in Kathmandu and airport transportation, are flawless and on time. This is one of the best trekking agencies in Nepal and their deluxe Mera Peak itinerary and service are the best. They truly offer a deluxe trek service. We highly recommend this company in Nepal. with best regards. David Hams", "country": "Calgary, Canada"}, {"id": 37, "date": "2024-11-20", "title": "Robins", "author": "5 star Mera peak Itinerary & comfort experience", "rating": 5, "comment": "I traveled to EBC two years ago with another company, but this time I found the Mera Peak package, which seemed affordable and suited my requirements. Pre-trip planning with Expert Representative was excellent, whether via email or WhatsApp. He is excellent at handling everything and was very welcoming. He did exactly what he promised. Our climbing guide, Pema Dorji, was perfect, and our porter, Dorji, was also great. The lodges along the way were upgraded, and I'm so happy that I could eat unlimited food and drinks. They even offered us a farewell cake, making the expedition the best experience ever. The well-being of the trekkers was always the top priority for the team at Nepal Trekking Tourism & Adventure. They are so professional in their service-it's truly a 5-star company. I will definitely use them for another trip and highly recommend them to anyone visiting Nepal.", "country": "Canada"}]	5.0	35	2026-10-23 20:31:04.764319+06
20	Deluxe Island Peak Expedition	deluxe-island-peak-expedition	17 Days Guided Himalayan Adventure	peak-climbing	Everest / Khumbu	peak-climbing-in-nepal	17	2599	2900	2699	3000	Challenging / Expedition	6,476m / 21,246ft	Spring (Mar-May) & Autumn (Sep-Nov)	4-Star City Hotel & Deluxe Attached-Bath Lodges	Full Board (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) on Trek	2 – 12 Guests (Private or Small Group)	f	peak	/images/upload/package/deluxe-island-peak-expedition.jpg	["/images/upload/package/slider/deluxe-island-peak-expedition.jpg"]	<p><span style="font-size:22px"><strong>Deluxe Island Peak Expedition-17&nbsp;days</strong></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="480"><span style="font-size:16px"><em>&quot;Only the best mountain adventure to hike Everest base camp + sunrise from Kala Patthar &amp; summit of Island Peak in one trip.&quot;</em></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="480"><span style="color:rgb(0, 128, 128)"><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Deluxe Island&nbsp;Peak Expedition Cost &ndash; 17-Day Full-Board Package</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul background-color:="" data-spread="false" font-size:="" inter="" pro="" segoe="" sf="" style="box-sizing: border-box; color: rgb(27, 42, 74); font-family: Inter, ">\r\n\t<li style="box-sizing: border-box;">\r\n\t<p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px 0px 1rem;"><span style="color:rgb(0, 128, 128)"><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Autumn Price (Mid-September to Mid-December):</strong> USD 2,599 per person.</span></span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li style="box-sizing: border-box;">\r\n\t<p style="box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px 0px 1rem;"><span style="color:rgb(0, 128, 128)"><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Spring Price (March to May):</strong> USD 2,777 per person.</span></span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="481"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>What is the Deluxe Island peak expedition &amp; what makes it Deluxe?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="482"><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe Island Peak Expedition is one of Nepal Trekking Tourism &amp; Adventure company&#39;s premier trekking and climbing special packages.This challenging adventure trek and expedition starts with warm and cultural sightseeing of the historical Kathmandu valley. After two days in Kathmandu, the real adventure of Deluxe Island peak climbing begins with an exciting 35-minute mountain flight to Tenzing Hillary Airport Lukla.Lukla Airport is the shortest and main gateway for all trekking and climbing trips in Everest National Park, which has more than 90 majestic peaks, including Mount Everest.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="483"><span style="font-size:16px">Right after landing at Lukla Airport, our adventure journey starts with a short and moderate level of trek to Phakding today, and the next day we trek to Namche Bazzar, the popular tourist hub for rest days at an altitude of 3440m, where most trekkers and climbers need to stay at least two nights for best acclimatization prior to heading toward further higher elevation. The second acclimatization day is at Pheriche at an altitude of approximately 4300m.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="484"><span style="font-size:16px">Island peak, the most famous and trekkers&#39; choice trekking peak situated at an altitude of 6160m, is the main target peak to summit during this itinerary of Deluxe Island peak climbing. In order to support full physical fitness and best acclimatization with weather, before the summit of Island peak, we will first complete a successful trek to Everest base camp (5364m) as well as Kala Patthar (5545m). So, climbing Island Peak also fulfills your dream trip to trek or hike to the base camp of the highest mountain in the world.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="485"><span style="font-size:16px">This deluxe island peak expedition includes trekking to Mount Everest base camp, Kala Patthar, and the summit of Nepal&#39;s most popular trekking peak.Technically moderately challenging, this trip needs good physical fitness and a little rock climbing or small mountain climbing experience can be helpful.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="486"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><strong><span style="font-size:18px">Why should you book the Deluxe Island Peak Expedition &amp; Everest Base Camp Trek with us?</span></strong></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul class="reduce-margin-block-end root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="487">\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">To enjoy the most comfortable deluxe lodges throughout the trip, including additional services and the best healthy foods,</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<ul class="reduce-margin-block-end root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="488">\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">In order to enjoy comfortable 4&nbsp;star or 5 star deluxe hotels in Kathmandu,</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<ul class="reduce-margin-block-end root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="489">\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">in order to experience the difference in high quality in service and a well prepared itinerary for a combined trip of island peak plus Everest base camp hiking.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<ul class="reduce-margin-block-end root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="490">\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">professional climbing and trekking guide and sherpa for a 100% successful trip.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="491"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Is this trekking and climbing for me? How difficult is this expedition?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="492"><span style="font-size:16px">This expedition requires good physical fitness for high-altitude trekking and climbing. You have to trek at least 5-8 hrs. a day and do two days of mountain climbing to reach the 6160m island peak. This expedition is therefore graded as a moderate-challenging trekking and climbing expedition. You have to prepare for this expedition with daily walking or hiking, and running of 1-2 hrs. after the expedition is booked.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="493"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>The best season for a Deluxe Island peak expedition:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="494"><span style="font-size:16px">We have two best seasons for trekking and island peak climbing trips. One of the best seasons is fall, from mid-September to mid-December. However, the best climbing and trekking periods are October and November. The spring season starts from March to May and the best period is from April to May. If you want to trek during the low season, the months of June to September are the least crowded with trekkers.</span></p>	Deluxe Island Peak Expedition-17 days "Only the best mountain adventure to hike Everest base camp + sunrise from Kala Patthar & summit of Island Peak in one trip." Deluxe Island Peak Expedition Cost - 17-Day Full-Board Package Autumn Price (Mid-September to Mid-December): USD 2,599 per person. Spring Price (March to May): USD 2,777 per person. What is the Deluxe Island peak expedition & what makes it Deluxe? Deluxe Island Peak Expedition is one of Nepal Trekking Tourism & Adventure company's premier trekking and climbing special packages.This challenging adventure trek and expedition starts with warm and cultural sightseeing of the historical Kathmandu valley. After two days in Kathmandu, the real adventure of Deluxe Island peak climbing begins with an exciting 35-minute mountain flight to Tenzing Hillary Airport Lukla.Lukla Airport is the shortest and main gateway for all trekking and climbing trips in Everest National Park, which has more than 90 majestic peaks, including Mount Everest. Right after landing at Lukla Airport, our adventure journey starts with a short and moderate level of trek to Phakding today, and the next day we trek to Namche Bazzar, the popular tourist hub for	<ol style="margin-left:40px">\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">The best peak climbing and trekking packages in Nepal&#39;s Everest region for unforgettable experiences</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">In a 17-day trip, you will trek to Everest base camp, sunrise hike to Kalapatthar, and climb the gorgeous island peak of Kalapatthar.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Stay at the most valuable deluxe lodges with hot shower facilities or the best available lodges along the trail.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">The itinerary is well prepared for safe and comfortable trekking and climbing.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Trek and climb with confidence because of a well acclimatized itinerary.</span></li>\r\n</ol>	<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif"><strong>Comfortable, deluxe accommodations and hygienic meals</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 4&nbsp;or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in Kathmandu on twin share with breakfast <span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>(2&nbsp;nights).</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>9 nights at a deluxe mountain lodge or guest house </strong></span>with an attached bathroom, including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>4 nights at the best selected lodge or guest house</strong></span> with a common bathroom including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>1 nights at Tented camp </strong></span>during climbing of Island peak</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">There are 3 hygienic vegetarian or non-vegetarian meals per day: breakfast, lunch, and dinner (you can choose meals from all over the Lodge every day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tea/coffee or other hot beverages during breakfast, lunch, and dinner (5&ndash;6 cups per day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">seasonal fruits and additional biscuit/cookies snacks&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Private transportation that is comfortable</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">All airport transfers by private, comfortable vehicle (international and domestic airport pick-up and drop-off as included in the itinerary).</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>baggage allowance and domestic flights.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="color:#800000"><strong><span style="font-size:14px">K<span style="font-size:16px">athmandu-Lukla-Kathmandu flight tickets</span></span></strong></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-size:16px">The baggage allowance on the Lukla flight is 15 kg, and we include 5 kg extra for free, for a total of 20 kg per person</span>.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Professional Private Expert Representatives &amp; porters</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">professional English-speaking tour guide for sightseeing in the city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A professional English-speaking guide for the trek</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Porter who is professional, dependable, helpful, and friendly (1 porter for every two people sharing)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Daily wage, lodging, meals, and guide and porter insurance.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Professional Island peak climbing Expert Representative, Insurance, climbing Bonus</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Extra porter for Island peak&nbsp;climbing for foods, tents, sleeping gears</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Trekking permits,peak climbing permits&nbsp;and entrance fees</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Entrance fees to all UNESCO heritage sites during city sightseeing</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Everest National Park Fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The local government fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekker&rsquo;s information management system (TIMS) fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Island peak climbing permit</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Island peak Permit Garbage deposit Management</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free information or guest services.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">guide to purchasing trekking clothing or equipment, as well as any other required wholesale shopping in Kathmandu.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support in the case of baggage loss or delay in Kathmandu from international flights to Nepal</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support to exchange money, get a local SIM card</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">24/7 emergency call support.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free safe baggage storage service during the trek</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free welcome dinner &amp; farewell professional body massage after the trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">We offer a free welcome Nepalese dinner with authentic Nepalese cultural dances on arrival day, or if you arrive late on arrival night, this will be provided on the second day.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">After the trek, you will receive a FREE 1-hour Ayurvedic full-body massage as a treatment for your tired body.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Other free services include:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A down sleeping bag and a down jacket are provided at no cost.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of water bottles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of trekking poles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of porter duffel bags (you can take them after the trek if you like).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">First Aid Kit</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking &amp; Island peak summited&nbsp;certificate</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking Map</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The company&#39;s gift</span></li>\r\n</ul>	<ul style="color: rgb(37, 37, 37);">\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Nepal Visa-US $ 50</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">International Flight to/from Kathmandu/home</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Travel and Emergency Helicopter Evacuation Insurance</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Meals (Lunch and Dinner) and other expenses while in Kathmandu (breakfast included at hotel)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Any soft drinks or alcoholic drinks during the trek, drinking water, battery charges, internet bills, dessert items, Except for breakfast, lunch, and dinner, extra tea/coffee or foods</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Laundry or personal expenses like internet WIFI, unforeseen costs due to natural disasters, sickness, flight delays, bad weather, urgent helicopter evacuation etc.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking gear and clothing</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tips for guides and porters</span></li>\r\n</ul>		[{"label": "1 Traveler (Solo Private)", "maxPax": 1, "minPax": 1, "deluxePrice": 2849, "luxuryPrice": 3049}, {"label": "2 – 3 Travelers", "maxPax": 3, "minPax": 2, "deluxePrice": 2599, "luxuryPrice": 2699}, {"label": "4 – 6 Travelers", "maxPax": 6, "minPax": 4, "deluxePrice": 2417, "luxuryPrice": 2510}, {"label": "7 – 12 Travelers (Group)", "maxPax": 12, "minPax": 7, "deluxePrice": 2261, "luxuryPrice": 2348}]	[{"day": 1, "meal": "FREE welcome Dinner", "title": "Day 01: Fly to Kathmandu Nepal, Warm welcome here in Kathmandu for Island peak Deluxe expedition, transfer to Hotel>> Deluxe Hotel( D)", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "1400m", "distance": "8-10 km drive", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe Hotel( D)", "transportation": "Private Car transfer to Hotel"}, {"day": 2, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner( B+L+D)", "title": "Day 02: You will drive to Airport early morning today to fly Lukla( 35 min) in first flight, then trek to Phakding(2610m)>> 4 hours>> 8 km>> Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "walking": "35 min flight + 4/5 hrs walking", "altitude": "2610 m", "distance": "8 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 3, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 03: Breakfast at 7 am, 6-7 hours Trek to Namche Bazzar( 3440m) today,Beautiful sherpa Land in Everest >> 10 km>> Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "walking": "6-7 hours trekking", "altitude": "3440m", "distance": "10 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 4, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 04: First Altitude Acclimatization at Namche, after breakfast we trek to Syangboche- Everest view hotel- Khumjung( 3790m) & Back to Namche overnight>> 5/6 km>>Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "walking": "3-4 hours Trekking", "altitude": "3440 m", "distance": "5-6 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 5, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 05: After Breakfast 7.30 am, we trek to Tengboche monastery visit and then trek down to Deboche( 3820m)>> 11 km>> 5/6 hours>>Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "walking": "5-6 hour Trekking", "altitude": "3820m", "distance": "11 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 6, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 06:  After Breakfast, We slowly Trek to Pheriche( 4371 m)>> 4/5 hours>> 8/9 km>>Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "walking": "4-5 hour Trekking", "altitude": "4371m", "di