istance": "18 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 11, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 11: short 3 hours trek to Chhukung( 4750m), Island peak gear preparation, light training with gears etc.. Best available Lodge( B+ L+ D)", "walking": "3 hours trek", "altitude": "4750 m", "distance": "4.5 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Best available Lodge( B+ L+ D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 12, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 12:  after breakfast we proceed toward island peak base camp(5100m), Preparation & Practice for summit>> 3-4 hours>> 5.6 km>> Tented camp( B+ L+D)", "walking": "3-4 hours trek", "altitude": "5100 m", "distance": "5.6 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Tented camp( B+ L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 13, "meal": "Breakfast + lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 13:  Midnight 2 am start walk/climbing, proceed to summit Island peak, reach Top of Island peak(6189 m) back to dingboche- deluxe lodge( B+L+D)", "walking": "9-10 hours", "altitude": "4750m", "distance": "14 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "deluxe lodge( B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 14, "meal": "Breakfast + lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 14:  we trek back to Namche today( 3820m)>> 7-9 hours>> Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "walking": "7-9 hours trek", "altitude": "3820m", "distance": "12.3 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 15, "meal": "Breakfast + lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 15:  Last day of trek: After breakfast you will trek to Lukla( 2860m)>> 7/8 hours>> 18 km- Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "walking": "7-8 hours Trekking", "altitude": "2860 m", "distance": "18 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 16, "meal": "Lavish Breakfast", "title": "Day 16: Early morning flight back to Kathmandu( 1400m), transfer to hotel, relax/rest/Laundry/shopping day in Kathmandu-  deluxe hotel( B+B)", "walking": "-", "altitude": "1400 m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "deluxe hotel( B+B)", "transportation": "35 min flights + Private car to Hotel"}, {"day": 17, "meal": "Lavish breakfast", "title": "Day 17: Deluxe Island peak expedition trip ends today... drive to Airport and fly your home.. SEE YOU again", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "1400 m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe Attached-Bath Lodge", "transportation": "Private car transfer to Airport"}]	[{"id": 247, "price": 2599, "status": 1, "endDate": "2026-12-01", "spotsLeft": 6, "startDate": "2026-11-15"}, {"id": 248, "price": 2599, "status": 1, "endDate": "2026-12-16", "spotsLeft": 9, "startDate": "2026-11-30"}]	[]	[{"id": 21, "date": "2022-07-26", "title": " Kevin", "author": "Deluxe Island Peak Expedition", "rating": 5, "comment": "Whoever it may concern, If you are searching for really high quality trekking to Everest and climbing services, then look no further than Expert Representative's company-Nepal trekking tourism & adventure. The deluxe Island Peak expedition is a perfectly planned itinerary, and all the lodges they offered us are upgraded ones with hot shower facilities as well as attached bathrooms. When you are in the high mountains, these types of lodge accommodation are very comfortable when you don't have to go out for a toilet. In many places throughout the trek, we are provided with rooms with attached toilet facilities. Besides the best accommodation, our guide, Nuru Jangbu, is a really professional Expert Representative who knows how to guide people on top of mountains. Our porters are so kind, supportive, and hard-working. Each lodge offers very healthy, fresh meals. and all other arrangements for the hotel in Kathmandu. Airport transfers are super and on time. We are provided a clean and warm sleeping bag and a down jacket without any extra cost. The free massage after the expedition was an added bonus of the whole trip, and the farewell cultural dinner was the best ending of the whole trip. Expert Representative is the best at communicating quickly via email or WhatsApp. From the arrival in Nepal to the final flight home, it was flawless service-truly a deluxe in the mountains. We would like to come back again for another expedition and would not hesitate to recommend it to anyone who wants to visit Nepal and would like to enjoy a really great trip like we had. Sincere thanks to Expert Representative, guide Nuru, and two other porters, Nima and Dorjee Sherpa, for the best trekking and deluxe climbing experience on an island peak in Nepal. Best regards, Kevin, NY, USA", "country": "NY, USA"}, {"id": 35, "date": "2024-11-20", "title": "Rabin T", "author": "Best deluxe island peak climbing package", "rating": 5, "comment": "Namaste Expert Representative, Thank you for checking in with us. Yes, we are back home after a wonderful 3-week trip to Nepal with your company. We had a great time and successfully summited Island Peak, thanks to the excellent guidance from our guide. The lodges were comfortable, the food was great, and we never experienced any issues with sickness or other problems. The deluxe Island Peak itinerary was perfect, and everything went smoothly. We look forward to our next peak adventure with you. I highly recommend Nepal Trekking Tourism & Adventure to anyone visiting Nepal.", "country": "Calgary, Canada"}]	5.0	19	2026-10-23 20:31:04.764319+06
2	Deluxe Annapurna Base Camp Trek	deluxe-annapurna-base-camp-trek	12 Days Guided Himalayan Adventure	deluxe-trekking	Annapurna	deluxe-nepal-trekking-tours	12	1644	1900	1744	2000	Moderate	5,416m (Thorong La) / 4,130m (ABC)	Spring (Mar-May) & Autumn (Sep-Nov)	4-Star City Hotel & Deluxe Attached-Bath Lodges	Full Board (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) on Trek	2 – 12 Guests (Private or Small Group)	f	bestseller	/images/upload/package/deluxe-annapurna-base-camp-trek.jpg	["/images/upload/package/slider/deluxe-annapurna-base-camp-trek.jpg"]	<h3><span style="font-size:22px"><strong>Deluxe Annapurna Base Camp Trek-12&nbsp;days-&nbsp;</strong></span><em><span style="font-size:16px">The most popular moderate level trekking in Nepal.</span></em></h3>\r\n\r\n<h4><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>What is the Deluxe Annapurna&nbsp;Base Camp Trek and what makes it Deluxe?</strong></span></span></h4>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="236"><span style="font-size:16px">Annapurna I (8091m) is the world&#39;s tenth tallest mountain, followed by Annapurna II, III, IV, and other Annapurna ranges such as Annapurna South.The trek to the base camp of these Annapurna ranges, from where climbers start climbing those peaks, is called Annapurna base camp. The Deluxe Annapurna Base Camp Trek is surrounded by dozens of snowy mountain ranges and is located 40 kilometers north of Pokhara in a high, glacial Himalayan trekking and hiking area. Under the supervision of ACAP (Annapurna conservation area project), this popular trek in the Annapurna region of Nepal is also known as the Annapurna sanctuary trek.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="237"><span style="font-size:16px">Situated at an altitude of 4130m, the Deluxe Annapurna Base Camp trek is the second busiest, fascinating, and moderate level of trek that combines the two most important trekking routes&mdash;<a href="https://www.nepaltrekkingtours.com/deluxe-mulde-peak-ghorepani-poonhill-trek">Ghorepani Poonhill</a> and Annapurna Base Camp. This trek is one of the nearest trekking trails from Pokhara city, from where you will drive in and drive out of the starting and ending points.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="237"><span style="font-size:16px">This trek is a low-price but high-value trekking package popularly known as the ABC Trek or Annapurna Sanctuary Trek, which is a highly upgraded version of lodges or guest houses on the trek. However, if your preference for trekking in Annapurna Base Camp is more best high-end lodges or guest houses, you can also find an optional trek package for the <a href="https://www.nepaltrekkingtours.com/luxury-annapurna-base-camp-trek">Annapurna Base Camp Luxury Trek.</a></span></p>\r\n\r\n<h4><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Why should you book a Deluxe Annapurna Base Camp Trek with us?</strong></span></span></h4>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="244"><span style="font-size:16px">There are a few reasons to book a deluxe Annapurna base camp trek with us.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="245"><span style="font-size:16px">In order to enjoy a comfortable, well-designed, and great value-oriented itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="245"><span style="font-size:16px">In order to stay in the best available deluxe lodges with attached bathrooms and hot showers,</span></li>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="245"><span style="font-size:16px">self-selected hygenic fresh meals during the trek.</span></li>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="245"><span style="font-size:16px">A professional Expert Representative and porter for whole trek</span></li>\r\n\t<li class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="245"><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe hotels, comfort transportation</span></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<h4><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Is this trek for me? How difficult is this trek?</strong></span></span></h4>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="240"><span style="font-size:16px">If you love local villages, mountains, rivers, and forest and would enjoy really beautiful trekking trails, this trek is absolutely for you. The Deluxe Annapurna Sanctuary Trek is a moderate-level trek that begins at 890m in Pokhara with a jeep ride to Thikhedunga, from which you hike up to Ghorepani Poonhill (3210m) and then to 4130m at Annapurna base camp. The best part of this trek is that you will start the trek from one place and end it in another.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="241"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>The best season for the Deluxe Annapurna Base Camp Trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="242"><span style="font-size:16px">Nepal has four distinct weather seasons: spring, summer (or monsoon), autumn, and winter. The best months for trekking in the Annapurna region are October to December, during the fall season, and early winter. Another recommended month in the spring season is March to May or until mid-June before the monsoon season starts from mid-June to mid-September.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="true" data-paragraphid="243">&nbsp;</p>	Deluxe Annapurna Base Camp Trek-12 days- The most popular moderate level trekking in Nepal. What is the Deluxe Annapurna Base Camp Trek and what makes it Deluxe? Annapurna I (8091m) is the world's tenth tallest mountain, followed by Annapurna II, III, IV, and other Annapurna ranges such as Annapurna South.The trek to the base camp of these Annapurna ranges, from where climbers start climbing those peaks, is called Annapurna base camp. The Deluxe Annapurna Base Camp Trek is surrounded by dozens of snowy mountain ranges and is located 40 kilometers north of Pokhara in a high, glacial Himalayan trekking and hiking area. Under the supervision of ACAP (Annapurna conservation area project), this popular trek in the Annapurna region of Nepal is also known as the Annapurna sanctuary trek. Situated at an altitude of 4130m, the Deluxe Annapurna Base Camp trek is the second busiest, fascinating, and moderate level of trek that combines the two most important trekking routes- Ghorepani Poonhill and Annapurna Base Camp. This trek is one of the nearest trekking trails from Pokhara city, from where you will drive in and drive out of the starting and ending points. This trek is a low-price but hig	<ol>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">one of the best mountain views in Annapurna, Nepal.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px">Trek with a moderate level of difficulty.</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px">The Annapurna Sanctuary trek is highly recommended.</span></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px">Ghorepani Poonhill and Annapurna Base Camp are two treks combined.</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px">Cultural tours of two famous cities: Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara</span></span></span></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px">Flights from Kathmandu-Pokhara-Kathmandu include flights to avoid road travel.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-size:18px">The start and ending point of each trek are different so that you can see new trails daily.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li>\r\n</ol>	<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif"><strong>Comfortable, deluxe accommodations and hygienic meals</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 4&nbsp;or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in <span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>KATHMANDU&nbsp;o</strong></span>n twin share with breakfast <span style="color:#8B4513">(<strong>2&nbsp;nights)</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 4&nbsp;or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in <span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>POKHARA</strong></span>&nbsp;on twin share with breakfast <span style="color:#800000">(<strong>1&nbsp;nights)</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:#800000"><strong>3 nights at a deluxe mountain lodge </strong></span>or guest house with an attached bathroom, including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>5 nights at the best selected lodge</strong></span> or guest house with a common bathroom including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">There are 3 hygienic vegetarian or non-vegetarian meals per day: breakfast, lunch, and dinner (you can choose meals from all over the Lodge every day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tea/coffee or other hot beverages during breakfast, lunch, and dinner (5&ndash;6 cups per day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">seasonal fruits and additional biscuit/cookies snacks&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Private transportation that is comfortable</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">private, comfortable vehicle tour of Pokhara City&nbsp;as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">All airport transfers by private, comfortable vehicle (international and domestic airport pick-up and drop-off as included in the itinerary).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>Pokhara- Pherdi &amp; Ulleri- Pokhara by Private Jee</strong></span>p( before/after trek)</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>baggage allowance and domestic flights.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="color:#2F4F4F"><strong><span style="font-size:14px">K<span style="font-size:16px">athmandu-Pokhara-Kathmandu flight tickets</span></span></strong></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-size:16px">The baggage allowance on the Pokhara&nbsp;flight is 15 kg, and we include 5 kg extra for free, for a total of 20 kg per person</span>.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Professional Private Expert Representatives &amp; porters</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">professional English-speaking tour guide for sightseeing in the city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A professional English-speaking guide for the trek</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Porter who is professional, dependable, helpful, and friendly (1 porter for every two people sharing)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Daily wage, lodging, meals, and guide and porter insurance.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Trekking permits and entrance fees</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Entrance fees to all UNESCO heritage sites during city sightseeing in Pokhara</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Annapurna conservation Area Project( ACAP)&nbsp;Entrance&nbsp;Fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The local government fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekker&rsquo;s information management system (TIMS) fee</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free information or guest services.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">guide to purchasing trekking clothing or equipment, as well as any other required wholesale shopping in Kathmandu.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support in the case of baggage loss or delay in Kathmandu from international flights to Nepal</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support to exchange money, get a local SIM card</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">24/7 emergency call support.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free safe baggage storage service during the trek</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free welcome dinner &amp; farewell professional body massage after the trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">We offer a free welcome Nepalese dinner with authentic Nepalese cultural dances on arrival day, or if you arrive late on arrival night, this will be provided on the second day.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">After the trek, you will receive a FREE 1-hour Ayurvedic full-body massage as a treatment for your tired body.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Other free services include:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A down sleeping bag and a down jacket are provided at no cost.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of water bottles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of trekking poles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of porter duffel bags (you can take them after the trek if you like).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">First Aid Kit</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking certificate</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking Map</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The company&#39;s gift</span></li>\r\n</ul>	<ul style="color: rgb(37, 37, 37);">\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Nepal Visa-US $ 50</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">International Flight to/from Kathmandu/home</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Travel and Emergency Helicopter Evacuation Insurance</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Meals (Lunch and Dinner) and other expenses while in Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara&nbsp;(breakfast included at hotel)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Any soft drinks or alcoholic drinks during the trek, drinking water, battery charges, internet bills, dessert items, Except for breakfast, lunch, and dinner, extra tea/coffee or foods</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Laundry or personal expenses like internet WIFI, unforeseen costs due to natural disasters, sickness, flight delays, bad weather, urgent heli