ture.", "country": "Indonesia"}, {"id": 44, "date": "2025-04-20", "title": "Clair", "author": "best Annapurna base camp trek", "rating": 5, "comment": "Amazing Trekking Experience! We had an unforgettable trek with Nepal Trekking Tourism & Adventure Company - everything was perfectly organized from start to finish. A big thank you to Expert Representative and the team for making our trip so smooth and memorable. Special thanks to our wonderful guide Mingmar and our hardworking porter Wangyal. Their support, kindness, and knowledge made the experience even better. The views, the people, and the adventure were beyond our expectations. We truly had the best experience of Nepal and can't wait to come back again! Clair, belgium", "country": "belgium"}, {"id": 45, "date": "2025-04-20", "title": "Wayne", "author": "Annapurna Base Camp Deluxe Trek – Amazing Experience", "rating": 5, "comment": "I had an unforgettable experience doing the Annapurna Base Camp Deluxe Trek with NETTA (Nepal Trekking Tourism & Adventure) . Everything was perfectly organized - a big thank you to Expert Representative for the top-notch service and seamless planning. Our guide Tasi Tamang was truly the best - knowledgeable, friendly, and always attentive. And a huge shoutout to Ngim a , our strong and cheerful porter who made the journey smooth and enjoyable. Beautiful trails, comfortable lodges, and an overall incredible adventure. Highly recommended to anyone looking for a high-quality trekking experience in Nepal! - Wayne, Belgium", "country": "spain"}]	5.0	16	2026-10-23 20:31:04.764319+06
9	 Deluxe Langtang Gosaikunda Lake Trek 	deluxe-langtang-gosaikunda-lake-trek	17 Days Guided Himalayan Adventure	deluxe-trekking	Langtang	deluxe-nepal-trekking-tours	17	1677	1900	1844	2100	Moderate	4,500m	Spring (Mar-May) & Autumn (Sep-Nov)	4-Star City Hotel & Deluxe Attached-Bath Lodges	Full Board (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) on Trek	2 – 12 Guests (Private or Small Group)	f	bestseller	/images/upload/package/new-project-17.jpg	["/images/upload/package/new-project-17.jpg", "/images/unsplash/photo-1518002054494-3a6f94352e9d-1200.jpg", "/images/unsplash/photo-1464822759023-fed622ff2c3b-1200.jpg"]	<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="330"><span style="font-size:22px"><strong>Deluxe Langtang Gosaikunda Lake trek-17 days&gt;&gt; </strong><em><span style="font-size:18px">The highly reccomended trek in Langtang region of Nepal</span></em></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>What is the Deluxe Langtang Gosaikunda Lake Trek and what makes it Deluxe?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="332"><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Deluxe The Langtang Gosaikunda Lake trek</strong>&nbsp;is a 17-day well-crafted itinerary for a deluxe trekking experience in the Langtang National Park of Nepal. We start this wonderful 17-day adventure trekking from Kathmandu to Syabrubesi by an overland drive of about 8&ndash;9 hours. The best experience of this whole trek is that you will start the trek from one place and end the trek at another place without repeating the same trekking trail. The route of the first week of this trek is normally known as the Langtang Valley Trek, where you will reach the highest point of Tserko Ri. Kyanjin Gomba is the last lodge area of this first week trek to enjoy magnificent views of the Himalayas.&nbsp; According to physical demand, this trek is moderate in level.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="333"><span style="font-size:16px">The second part of this luxury trek in the Langtang region is the Gosaikunda lake trek, popularly known as the abode of the Hindu deities Shiva and Gauri. This holy lake is located at an altitude of 4380m and offers the best Himalayan views. The rest of the trek is after Gosaikunda lake. The next trekking area is the Helambu valley, with typical villages and culture of the Helambu people. The trek leads you to Shivapuri national park, the closest national park to Kathmandu city. The last days of the trek around Chisapani, which is the finest hilly area of Kathmandu, offer one of the great views of mountains.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="334"><span style="font-size:16px">Overall, this is a combination of four short treks in one 17-day deluxe trek in the Langtang trekking area: Langtang valley, Gosaikunda lake, Helambu trek, and Chisapani trek. You will enjoy the most beautiful trekking holidays in two national parks of Nepal: Langtang National Park and Shivapuri National Park. The accommodation on the whole trek is not too luxurious but, in many places, we can offer deluxe lodges or guesthouses throughout the trek.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Why should you book a Deluxe Langtang Gosaikunda Lake Trek with us?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="341"><span style="font-size:16px">&gt;&gt;Enjoy a well-designed and best-value itinerary in the Langtang trekking area.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="342"><span style="font-size:16px">&gt;&gt;To experience the best-selected lodges with hot showers and attached bath room facilities, whenever they are available.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="true" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="343"><span style="font-size:16px">&gt;&gt;To enjoy high quality, fresh and hygenic nepali cuisines during the trek</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="true" data-from-init="true" data-paragraphid="344"><span style="font-size:16px">&gt;&gt;To enjoy best personalized trekking service from local guides and porter</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Is this trekking for me? How difficult is the Deluxe Langtang Gosaikunda lake trek?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="337"><span style="font-size:16px">Geographically, this trekking trail is not that demanding. You will enjoy the best experience of this trek at an altitude of less than 5000m in the whole trekking period. The daily trekking or hiking time is about 6&ndash;8 hours a day, which is not too long. Previous trekking experience will be supported for this trek, but all fresher trekkers may join this trek. Physical fitness training of daily walking, jogging, or running has extra advantages. Any aged group can do this trek.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="true" data-paragraphid="338"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>The best season for the Deluxe Langtang Gosaikunda lake trek:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="340"><span style="font-size:16px">Nepal offers basically 4 weather seasons: winter, spring, summer (or monsoon) and autumn. Summer and winter months are normally not recommended for trekking, and so two seasons&mdash;Spring and Autumn&mdash;offer nice trekking and hiking seasons. So the best months for trekking are October-December and March-May.</span></p>\r\n	Deluxe Langtang Gosaikunda Lake trek-17 days&gt;&gt; The highly reccomended trek in Langtang region of Nepal What is the Deluxe Langtang Gosaikunda Lake Trek and what makes it Deluxe? Deluxe The Langtang Gosaikunda Lake trek is a 17-day well-crafted itinerary for a deluxe trekking experience in the Langtang National Park of Nepal. We start this wonderful 17-day adventure trekking from Kathmandu to Syabrubesi by an overland drive of about 8-9 hours. The best experience of this whole trek is that you will start the trek from one place and end the trek at another place without repeating the same trekking trail. The route of the first week of this trek is normally known as the Langtang Valley Trek, where you will reach the highest point of Tserko Ri. Kyanjin Gomba is the last lodge area of this first week trek to enjoy magnificent views of the Himalayas. According to physical demand, this trek is moderate in level. The second part of this luxury trek in the Langtang region is the Gosaikunda lake trek, popularly known as the abode of the Hindu deities Shiva and Gauri. This holy lake is located at an altitude of 4380m and offers the best Himalayan views. The rest of the trek is after Gos	<ol>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">The best 17 days of trekking in Langtang National Park, Nepal</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Trekking in Langtang Valley, Gosaikunda Lake, Helambu Valley, and Chisapani.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Enjoy the best selected eco-lodges for a comfortable stay and healthy meals daily.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">A cultural tour in the Kathmandu Valley</span></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n	<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif"><strong>Comfortable, deluxe accommodations and hygienic meals</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 3 or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in Kathmandu on twin share with breakfast (<span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>3&nbsp;nights).</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>13 nights at the best selected lodge or guest house</strong></span> with a common bathroom including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">There are 3 hygienic vegetarian or non-vegetarian meals per day: breakfast, lunch, and dinner (you can choose meals from all over the Lodge every day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tea/coffee or other hot beverages during breakfast, lunch, and dinner (5&ndash;6 cups per day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">seasonal fruits and additional biscuit/cookies snacks&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Private transportation that is comfortable</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">private, comfortable vehicle tour of Kathmandu city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">All airport transfers by private, comfortable vehicle (international and domestic airport pick-up and drop-off as included in the itinerary).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><strong><span style="color:#8B4513"><span style="font-size:16px">Kathmandu- Syabrubesi by Private Jeep( before trek)</span></span></strong></li>\r\n\t<li><strong><span style="color:#8B4513"><span style="font-size:16px">SundariJal- Kathmandu by Private car( after trek)</span></span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Professional Private Expert Representatives &amp; porters</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">professional English-speaking tour guide for sightseeing in the city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A professional English-speaking guide for the trek</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Porter who is professional, dependable, helpful, and friendly (1 porter for every two people sharing)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Daily wage, lodging, meals, and guide and porter insurance.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Trekking permits and entrance fees</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Entrance fees to all UNESCO heritage sites during city sightseeing</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Langtang National Park Fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The local government fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekker&rsquo;s information management system (TIMS) fee</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free information or guest services.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">guide to purchasing trekking clothing or equipment, as well as any other required wholesale shopping in Kathmandu.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support in the case of baggage loss or delay in Kathmandu from international flights to Nepal</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support to exchange money, get a local SIM card</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">24/7 emergency call support.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free safe baggage storage service during the trek</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free welcome dinner &amp; farewell professional body massage after the trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">We offer a free welcome Nepalese dinner with authentic Nepalese cultural dances on arrival day, or if you arrive late on arrival night, this will be provided on the second day.</span></li>\r\n\t<li>