inner is so nice, and after the trek, massage is the best gift for tired bodies from the trek. All these nice services made the Langtang Gosaikunda lake trek truly a deluxe one. We look forward to seeing you and your guide for the next trek. Regards, Thomas L.", "country": "Denmark"}]	5.0	32	2026-10-23 20:31:04.764319+06
31	Luxury Helicopter Everest Base Camp Trek	luxury-helicopter-everest-base-camp-trek	12 Days Guided Himalayan Adventure	luxury-trekking	Everest	luxury-nepal-trekking-tours	12	3895	4300	5258	5843	Moderate	5,545m (Kala Patthar)	Spring (Mar-May) & Autumn (Sep-Nov)	5-Star City Hotels & Luxury Mountain Lodges	Full Board (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) on Trek	2 – 12 Guests (Private or Small Group)	t	luxury	/images/upload/package/luxury-helicopter-everest-base-camp-trek.jpg	["/images/upload/package/slider/luxury-helicopter-everest-base-camp-trek.jpg"]	<h3><span style="font-size:22px"><strong>Luxury Helicopter Everest base camp trek- 12 days</strong></span></h3>\r\n\r\n<h4><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>What is the Luxury Helicopter Everest&nbsp;Base Camp Trek &amp; what makes it luxury?</strong></span></span></h4>\r\n\r\n<div class="flex max-w-full flex-col flex-grow">\r\n<div class="min-h-8 text-message flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 whitespace-normal break-words [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="32326780-6109-471f-83c4-ca789b70f8fd" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4o-mini" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]">\r\n<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light">\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">The Luxury Helicopter Everest Base Camp Trek is CCC Nepal Trekking Tours&#39; premier trekking package, designed to provide the ultimate experience for those wishing to explore the majestic Everest region. This 12-day trek combines adventure with comfort, allowing you and your family to reach the iconic Everest Base Camp and Kala Patthar&mdash;one of the most famous hiking destinations in the world.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h4><span style="font-size:16px">What Makes It Luxury?</span></h4>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Top-Class Accommodations</strong>:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">You will stay in Nepal&rsquo;s finest luxury hotels in Kathmandu and the best lodges in the Everest region, including renowned options like Yeti Mountain Home. These accommodations provide exceptional service and comfort, ensuring a relaxing stay.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Helicopter Return</strong>:</span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">After reaching both Everest Base Camp and Kala Patthar, you&rsquo;ll return to Kathmandu by helicopter from Lukla. This option saves you time and energy, making the journey more comfortable and efficient.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Personalized Service</strong>:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Throughout the trek, you will receive attentive and personalized service from experienced guides and support staff dedicated to making your adventure enjoyable.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Streamlined Itinerary</strong>:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The trek follows a well-structured itinerary that balances trekking with relaxation, allowing you to fully appreciate the stunning scenery and rich culture of the region.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Exclusive Experiences</strong>:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Enjoy unique experiences along the way, such as fine dining at high-quality lodges and opportunities to immerse yourself in local culture, all while surrounded by breathtaking Himalayan views.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">The Luxury Helicopter Everest Base Camp Trek offers an exceptional way to realize your dream of standing at the foot of Mount Everest. With luxurious accommodations, outstanding service, and the convenience of helicopter transport, this trek ensures a memorable adventure in the heart of the Himalayas. Perfect for families and discerning travelers, it combines the thrill of trekking with the comfort and elegance of a luxury experience.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><strong>Why choose us for a Luxury Helicopter Everest Base Camp Trek?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">Here are five compelling reasons to book your luxury trek with us:</span></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Unique and Authentic Experience</strong>:<br />\r\n\tEnjoy one of the most unique, authentic, and luxurious trekking experiences in Nepal&#39;s Everest region. We focus on providing a blend of adventure and comfort, ensuring that your journey is truly memorable.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Luxurious Accommodations</strong>:<br />\r\n\tStay in the most luxurious hotels and lodges in Nepal, where comfort and exceptional service are guaranteed. Our carefully selected accommodations offer the perfect retreat after a day of trekking.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Helicopter Mountain Flight</strong>:<br />\r\n\tExperience a once-in-a-lifetime helicopter mountain flight around Mount Everest and other 8,000-meter peaks. This breathtaking journey allows you to take in stunning views from above, adding an extraordinary element to your trek.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Hygienic Cuisine</strong>:<br />\r\n\tEnjoy the best hygienic cuisine during your trek, with meals prepared to the highest standards. We prioritize your health and satisfaction, ensuring that you have nourishing and delicious food throughout your journey.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Expert Local Expert Representatives</strong>:<br />\r\n\tBenefit from the highest quality trekking service provided by our expert local Expert Representatives, who bring over 25 years of experience. Their knowledge and expertise will enhance your trek, ensuring safety, comfort, and cultural insights along the way.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">Choosing us for your Luxury Helicopter Everest Base Camp Trek means embracing an unparalleled adventure filled with comfort, expert guidance, and unforgettable experiences. Let us help you create lasting memories in the stunning Everest region!</span></p>\r\n\r\n<div class="flex max-w-full flex-col flex-grow">\r\n<div class="min-h-8 text-message flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 whitespace-normal break-words [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="176874e0-2276-42e6-85ee-dd8ab06cd021" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4o-mini" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]">\r\n<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light">\r\n<h3><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="color:#B22222"><strong>Is This Trekking for Me? How Difficult is the Luxury Everest Base Camp&nbsp;Helicopter&nbsp;Trek?</strong></span></span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">The highest altitude on this trek is <strong>Kala Patthar</strong>, reaching <strong>5,644 meters</strong>, while the second highest point is <strong>Everest Base Camp</strong> at <strong>5,364 meters</strong>. Trekking above <strong>5,000 meters</strong> is rated as a demanding trek, but it is not overly challenging.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">This itinerary is the shortest option available; however, it includes <strong>two acclimatization days</strong> at altitudes of <strong>3,440 meters</strong> and <strong>4,300 meters</strong>. These acclimatization days are essential for preventing unnecessary Acute Mountain Sickness (AMS).</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">While previous trekking experience is advantageous, all new trekkers are welcome to participate. To successfully complete this trek, you simply need to be <strong>physically fit</strong> and prepared to trek for a minimum of <strong>4 hours</strong> to a maximum of <strong>6-7 hours</strong> each day.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">If you are in good physical condition and ready for a rewarding adventure, the Luxury Helicopter Everest Base Camp Trek is suitable for you. With proper acclimatization and support, you can enjoy this incredible journey to one of the world&#39;s most iconic destinations.</span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class="mb-2 flex gap-3 empty:hidden -ml-2">\r\n<div class="items-center justify-start rounded-xl p-1 flex">\r\n<div class="flex items-center">\r\n<div class="flex items-center pb-0"><span style="color:#B22222"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>The best time to trek to Everest base camp by luxury helicopter:</strong></span></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="139"><span style="font-size:16px">The best months for this luxury trekking experience, considering the best weather, are October, November, and December. The second-best month in the spring season is March, followed by April and May. The monsoon season starts in Nepal in mid-June and ends by mid-September, so during these three months, the weather is not great. The trekking season begins in September, which means there are fewer hikers on the trail.</span></p>	Luxury Helicopter Everest base camp trek- 12 days What is the Luxury Helicopter Everest Base Camp Trek & what makes it luxury? The Luxury Helicopter Everest Base Camp Trek is CCC Nepal Trekking Tours' premier trekking package, designed to provide the ultimate experience for those wishing to explore the majestic Everest region. This 12-day trek combines adventure with comfort, allowing you and your family to reach the iconic Everest Base Camp and Kala Patthar-one of the most famous hiking destinations in the world. What Makes It Luxury? Top-Class Accommodations : You will stay in Nepal's finest luxury hotels in Kathmandu and the best lodges in the Everest region, including renowned options like Yeti Mountain Home. These accommodations provide exceptional service and comfort, ensuring a relaxing stay. Helicopter Return : After reaching both Everest Base Camp and Kala Patthar, you'll return to Kathmandu by helicopter from Lukla. This option saves you time and energy, making the journey more comfortable and efficient. Personalized Service : Throughout the trek, you will receive attentive and personalized service from experienced guides and support staff dedicated to making your adventure e	<p><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Highlights of the Luxury Helicopter Everest Base Camp Trek</strong></span></p>\r\n\r\n<div class="flex max-w-full flex-col flex-grow">\r\n<div class="min-h-8 text-message flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 whitespace-normal break-words [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="64691412-ff2c-4c6c-b8e1-0ac92f338ea0" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4o-mini" dir="auto">\r\n<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]">\r\n<div class="markdown prose w-full break-words dark:prose-invert light">\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Most Luxurious Trek</strong>: Experience the ultimate comfort on the shortest version of the Everest Base Camp trek in Nepal.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Top-Quality Accommodations</strong>: Enjoy all nights in luxurious lodges throughout the trek, along with a stay at the prestigious five-star Hotel Dwarika in Kathmandu.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Helicopter Return</strong>: Save time and enhance your comfort by flying back to Lukla from Gorakshep after your unforgettable hikes to Everest Base Camp and Kala Patthar.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Breathtaking Views</strong>: Take in the most scenic mountain and valley views during your helicopter ride from Gorakshep to Lukla, creating memories that will last a lifetime.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Extraordinary Experience</strong>: Join this luxury helicopter trek and reward yourself with the feeling of being an elite trekker.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Once-in-a-Lifetime Journey</strong>: Experience our highest class of luxury trekking packages, designed for a journey that is truly unforgettable.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Best Value Adventure</strong>: Enjoy the best value trekking adventure for an exceptional holiday in Nepal.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>	<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif"><strong>Comfortable, deluxe accommodations and hygienic meals</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Luxury&nbsp;5-star (<strong>Marriot</strong><span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong><strong>&nbsp;</strong>Hotel)</strong></span></span>&nbsp;Hotel accommodation in Kathmandu on twin share with breakfast<span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>&nbsp;(2&nbsp;nights).</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">4 nights at a Luxury&nbsp;mountain lodge (<span style="font-size:18px"><span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><strong>&nbsp;MLN Yeti Mountain Home- YMH)&nbsp;</strong></span><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>in PHAKDING( 1 night), NAMCHE( 2&nbsp;nights) &amp; LUKLA( 1 night)</strong></span></span><span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span>with an attached bathroom, including hot shower.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">2 nights at a Deluxe&nbsp;mountain lodge (<span style="font-size:18px"><span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><strong>&nbsp;Hotel Tashi delek dingbo</strong></span></span></span><span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><strong><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:google sans,arial,sans-serif">che or Dingboche resort</span></span></strong></span><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><strong>) in DINGBOCHE( 2&nbsp;nights)</strong></span></span>&nbsp;with an attached bathroom, including hot&nbsp;shower.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">1 night&nbsp;at the Deluxe guest house(&nbsp;<span style="font-size:18px"><span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><strong>Himalayan Culture home or Rivendell&nbsp;lodge</strong></span>)</span>&nbsp;at <strong>DEBOCHE</strong>&nbsp;with a attached&nbsp;bathroom including hot&nbsp;shower.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">1 night&nbsp;at the Best available &amp; selected Lodge(&nbsp;<span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>N<span style="font-size:18px">ew EBC Guest house or Oxygen altitude home</span></strong></span>) at <strong>LOBUCHE</strong>&nbsp;with a common&nbsp;bathroom including hot shower.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">1 night&nbsp;at the Best available &amp; selected Lodge( <strong>Snow land lodge or Buddha Lodge</strong><span style="font-size:18px">)</span>&nbsp;at <strong>GORAKSHEP&nbsp;</strong>with a shared&nbsp;bathroom&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">There are 3 hygienic vegetarian or non-vegetarian meals per day: breakfast, lunch, and dinner (you can choose meals from all over the Lodge every day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tea/coffee or other hot beverages during breakfast, lunch, and dinner (5&ndash;6 cups per day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">seasonal fruits and additional biscuit/cookies snacks&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Wifi is available for free in the lodges.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">4-5 liters of free boiled or purified water</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Mobile/camera/laptop battery charges&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p style="color: #252525;">&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p style="color: #252525;"><u><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><strong>After Everest Base Camp and the Kala Patthar trek, take a helicopter flight from Gorakshep to Lukla.</strong></span></span></u></p>\r\n\r\n<ul style="color: #252525;">\r\n\t<li><strong><span style="font-size:18px">A Private Helicopter from Gorakshep to Lukla</span></strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Private transportation that is comfortable</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">private, comfortable vehicle tour of Kathmandu city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">All airport transfers by private, comfortable vehicle (international and domestic airport pick-up and drop-off as included in the itinerary).</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>baggage allowance and domestic flights.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:14px">K<span style="font-size:16px">athmandu-Lukla-Kathmandu flight tickets</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-size:16px">The baggage allowance on the Lukla flight is 15 kg, and we include 5 kg extra for free, for a total of 20 kg per person</span>.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Professional Private Expert Representatives &amp; porters</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">professional English-speaking tour guide for sightseeing in the city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A professional English-speaking guide for the trek</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Porter who is professional, dependable, helpful, and friendly (1 porter for every two people sharing)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Daily wage, lodging, meals, and guide and porter insurance.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Trekking permits and entrance fees</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Entrance fees to all UNESCO heritage sites during city sightseeing</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Everest National Park Fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The local government fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekker&rsquo;s information management system (TIMS) fee</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free information or guest services.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">guide to purchasing trekking clothing or equipment, as well as any other required wholesale shopping in Kathmandu.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support in the case of baggage loss or delay in Kathmandu from international flights to Nepal</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support to exchange money, get a local SIM card</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">24/7 emergency call support.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free safe baggage storage service during the trek</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free welcome dinner &amp; farewell professional body massage after the trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">We offer a free welcome Nepalese dinner with authentic Nepalese cultural dances on arrival day, or if you arrive late on arrival night, this will be provided on the second day.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">After the trek, you will receive a FREE 1-hour Ayurvedic full-body massage as a treatment for your tired body.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Other free services include:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A down sleeping bag and a down jacket are provided at no cost.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of water bottles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of trekking poles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of porter duffel bags (you can take them after the trek if you like).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">First Aid Kit</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking certificate</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking Map</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The company&#39;s gift</span></li>\r\n</ul>	<ul style="color: rgb(37, 37, 37);">\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Nepal Visa-US $ 50</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">International Flight to/from Kathmandu/home</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Travel and Emergency Helicopter Evacuation Insurance</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Meals (Lunch and Dinner) and other expenses while in Kathmandu (breakfast included at hotel)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Any soft drinks or alcoholic drinks during the trek,internet bills, dessert items, Except for breakfast, lunch, and dinner, extra tea/coffee or foods</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Laundry or personal expenses like internet WIFI, unforeseen costs due to natural disasters, sickness, flight delays, bad weather, urgent helicopter evacuation etc.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking gear and clothing</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tips for guides and porters</span></li>\r\n</ul>		[{"label": "1 Traveler (Solo Private)", "maxPax": 1, "minPax": 1, "deluxePrice": 4145, "luxuryPrice": 2949}, {"label": "2 – 3 Travelers", "maxPax": 3, "minPax": 2, "deluxePrice": 3895, "luxuryPrice": 2599}, {"label": "4 – 6 Travelers", "maxPax": 6, "minPax": 4, "deluxePrice": 3622, "luxuryPrice": 2417}, {"label": "7 – 12 Travelers (Group)", "maxPax": 12, "minPax": 7, "deluxePrice": 3389, "luxuryPrice": 2261}]	[{"day": 1, "meal": "FREE welcome Dinner", "title": "Day 01: You are warm welcome in Kathmandu Airport for Luxury EBC Helicopter trek and Private CAR transfer to Hotel Marriot( D)", "walking": "-", "altitude": "1400m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Hotel Marriot", "transportation": "Private Car"}, {"day": 2, "meal": "Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner (B+L+D)", "title": "Day 2", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "3,440m / 11,286ft", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "5-Star Luxury Mountain Lodge", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 3, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner( B+L+D)", "title": "Day 02: Your Luxury EBC trek start with Flight to Lukla( 35 min) & then your first Luxury trek to Phakding (2610m) or Monjo-4/5 hrs- MLN Yeti Mountain Home( B + L+ D)", "walking": "35 min flight + 4/5 hrs walking", "altitude": "2610m", "distance": "8 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "MLN Yeti Mountain Home( B + L+ D)", "transportation": "Private car + flights + Trek 4 hours"}, {"day": 4, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 03:  Second day Luxury EBC Helicopter trekking to Namche Bazaar (3440M / 11283F), 7-8 hrs- MLN Yeti Mountain Home( B + L+ D)", "walking": "6-7 hours trekking", "altitude": "3440m", "distance": "10 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "MLN Yeti Mountain Home( B + L+ D)", "transportation": "-"}, {"day": 5, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 04: First Acclimatization hiking to Everest view hotel & Khumjung Village( 3790m), back to Namche for overnight- MLN Yeti Mountain Home( B + L+ D)", "walking": "3-4 hours Trekking", "altitude": "3440", "distance": "6 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "MLN Yeti Mountain Home( B + L+ D)", "transportation": "-"}, {"day": 6, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B/L/D)", "title": "Day 05: 4th day Trek to Deboche (3820M /12529F) via Tengboche Monastery hrs- Himalayan Culture Home or Rivendell Lodge (B/L/D)", "walking": "5-6 hour Trekking", "altitude": "3820m", "distance": "11 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Himalayan Culture Home or Rivendell Lodge  (B/L/D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 7, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B/L/D)", "title": "Day 06: 5th day Luxury Trek from Deboche to Dingboche (4410m /14,465 ft)- 4 hrs-  Hotel Tashidelek Dingboche or Dingboche Resort (B/L/D)", "walking": "4-5 hour Trekking", "altitude": "4371m", "distance": "8 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Hotel Tashidelek Dingboche or Dingboche Resort (B/L/D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 8, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B/L/D)", "title": "Day 07: Second Acclimatization day at Dingboche, Acclimatization trek to Nagarjun Hill( 5000m) and return- 5 hrs- Hotel Tashidelek Dingboche or Dingboche Resort (B/L/D)", "walking": "4-5 hours Trekking", "altitude": "4371m", "distance": "12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Hotel Tashidelek Dingboche or Dingboche Resort (B/L/D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 9, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B/L/D)", "title": "Day 08: Seventh day Luxury Trek from Dingboche to Lobuche (4940M/ 16105F) - 4/5 hrs- Oxygen altitude home or New EBC guest house (B/L/D)", "walking": "4- 5 hours Trekking", "altitude": "4940m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Oxygen altitude home or New EBC guest house (B/L/D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 10, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B/L/D)", "title": "Day 09: Eighth day Luxury EBC helicopter Trek from Lobuche to Everest base camp (5364M/17594F)- Gorakshep (5140M/ 16860F)-8/9 hrs-Snow land Lodge or Buddha lodge (B/L/D)", "walking": "8-9 hour trekking", "altitude": "5170m", "distance": "10km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Snow land Lodge or Buddha lodge (B/L/D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 11, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B/L/D)", "title": "Day 10:  Last day hike to Kalapattar (5643M) early morning for sunrise view, back to Gorakshep & Helicopter flight back to Lukla- MLN Yeti Mountain Home( B + L+ D)", "walking": "5-6 hours Trekking", "altitude": "2860m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "MLN Yeti Mountain Home( B + L+ D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 12, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Day 11: Lukla to Kathmandu( 35 min) early flight & Transfer to Hotel, Half day city tour( 3/4 hrs) - Hotel Marriot(B/B)", "walking": "Half day city tour by Car", "altitude": "1400", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Hotel Marriot", "transportation": "Flights + Private car"}, {"day": 13, "meal": "breakfast", "title": "Day 12:  Last day of Your Luxury Everest base camp helicopter trek, fly to home today- SEE YOU AGAIN", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "3,440m / 11,286ft", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "-", "transportation": "Private Car Transfer to Airport"}]	[{"id": 31, "price": 3895, "status": "Guaranteed", "endDate": "2026-11-15", "spotsLeft": 6, "startDate": "2026-11-01"}, {"id": 32, "price": 3895, "status": "Available", "endDate": "2026-11-29", "spotsLeft": 8, "startDate": "2026-11-15"}, {"id": 33, "price": 3895, "status": "Available", "endDate": "2026-12-19", "spotsLeft": 10, "startDate": "2026-12-05"}, {"id": 34, "price": 3895, "status": "Available", "endDate": "2027-03-24", "spotsLeft": 12, "startDate": "2027-03-10"}, {"id": 35, "price": 3895, "status": "Guaranteed", "endDate": "2027-04-16", "spotsLeft": 5, "startDate": "2027-04-02"}]	[]	[{"id": 4, "date": "2022-07-22", "title": "Robert", "author": "Everest base camp by Helicopter", "rating": 5, "comment": "Hello Expert Representative, Thanks for your email after our return home. We reached home and would like to thank you a lot for all the best service you have provided during our Nepal trip. We had a awesome vacation in Nepal. Every little service was handled well. Your guide, Rinji, is perfect and the porter is very helpful. The lodges you have booked are very nice. The helicopter ride back after the trek was enjoyable and it was nice to return to Lukla by helicopter rather than walk back the same route. Thanks for all your great service. It was a great trip. Sincerely, Robert", "country": "USA"}, {"id": 57, "date": "2025-04-20", "title": "Richard", "author": "Perfect Short & Luxury Everest Base Camp Trek ", "rating": 5, "comment": "I've wanted to do the Everest Base Camp trek for a long time, but I was specifically looking for a shorter and more comfortable option. After some research, I found that CCC Nepal Trekking Tours offers a 12-day Luxury Everest Base Camp trek with a helicopter return to Kathmandu - and it was exactly what I was looking for! To be honest, the trek wasn't easy - we faced some bad weather conditions, and our flight to Lukla was canceled. But Expert Representative acted immediately and arranged a shared helicopter to Lukla, saving us precious time since my schedule was tight. His quick thinking and excellent organization truly made a difference. Our guide, Pema Dorji, was fantastic - passionate, caring, and always attentive. Our porter stayed close behind us throughout the trek, always ensuring we were doing well and had everything we needed. The lodges during the trek were top-class luxury, just as promised in the itinerary. The food and drink options were excellent - I could choose whatever I wanted, and there was always plenty of it. Every detail was thoughtfully planned to ensure maximum comfort. Even before the trek began, Expert Representative was incredibly responsive - always quick to reply with accurate information and helpful planning tips. He personally welcomed me at the airport and hosted a wonderful welcome dinner on the first evening. This trek was everything I hoped for and more. I highly recommend this 12-day luxury EBC trek with helicopter return to anyone looking for a shorter, high-comfort trekking adventure in Nepal. Richard, USA", "country": "canada"}, {"id": 58, "date": "2025-04-20", "title": "Jim", "author": "Premium Everest Trek – Worth Every Penny", "rating": 5, "comment": "To be honest, this was the most expensive Everest trek I've done, but also the most comfortable . I've been to Nepal five times, and this time I chose to trek with Expert Representative - and it was the right choice. I always prefer rooms with private bathrooms and hot showers, and this trek delivered that for most nights. While Lobuche and Gorakshep (above 5,000m) don't have hot water, the lodges are still the best available. Lodges up to Deboche were very comfortable, and Dingboche was nice, though not the top. The luxury lodges, excellent meals, and top-class hotel in Kathmandu made it all worthwhile. Our guide Mingmar and the porter were both fantastic. Expert Representative is a true expert in organizing luxury treks in Nepal , and I highly recommend his company to anyone looking for a premium experience. Jim, Hong Kong", "country": "hongkong"}, {"id": 65, "date": "2025-04-20", "title": "Alex", "author": "The Best Luxury Helicopter Everest base camp trek", "rating": 5, "comment": "Namaste Expert Representative and Team, After completing our Everest Base Camp trek in October 2024, we are now back to work, but the memories of our journey in Nepal are still fresh in our hearts. On behalf of myself and my wife, we want to say a big thank you for your wonderful hospitality and excellent trekking services. The Luxury Everest Base Camp Trek with helicopter return was the perfect choice for us. Our guide Mingmar and assistant guide Norbu were both young, kind, caring, and extremely helpful throughout the trek. Our porter was also incredibly supportive and friendly. The hotel in Kathmandu and all the lodges on the trail were exactly as described in your itinerary - clean, comfortable, and welcoming. We especially appreciated the helicopter return after reaching EBC and Kalapatthar - it was a fantastic option, particularly for my wife, as we were quite tired by then. It made the end of our trek much easier and more enjoyable. Overall, we had a truly amazing experience, and we're already thinking about coming back for another adventure with your team. Thank you once again for an unforgettable trek in Nepal! With best regards, Alex, Australia", "country": "Australia"}]	5.0	31	2026-10-23 20:31:04.764319+06
36	Luxury Everest Experience Trek	luxury-everest-experience-trek	7 Days Guided Himalayan Adventure	luxury-trekking	Everest	luxury-nepal-trekking-tours	7	2633	3000	3555	3950	Easy to Moderate	5,545m (Kala Patthar)	Spring (Mar-May) & Autumn (Sep-Nov)	5-Star City Hotels & Luxury Mountain Lodges	Full Board (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) on Trek	2 – 12 Guests (Private or Small Group)	f	luxury	/images/upload/package/luxury-everest-experience-trek.jpg	["/images/upload/package/slider/luxury-everest-experience-trek.jpg"]	<p><span style="font-size:20px"><strong>Luxury Everest Experience Trek - 7 Days</strong></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">Want to see Mount Everest in the shortest timeframe without a strenuous trek? Interested in an easy to moderate-level trek but worried about the quality of accommodation and food during the journey?</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#B22222"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>What is the Luxury Everest view&nbsp;Trek and What Makes It Luxury?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">Our <strong>Luxury Everest Experience Trek </strong>addresses all your desires and requirements, fulfilling your thrill for a short and moderate trek at its best. This one-week trek in the Everest region invites you to spend nights in top-quality luxury lodges, such as mountain lodges of Nepal formerly known as Yeti Mountain Home, and enjoy a stay at a top 5-star hotel dwarika in Kathmandu.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">The <strong>Luxury Everest view&nbsp;Trek</strong> will guide you to the famous Everest View Hotel and the beautiful Khumjung Village above Namche, home to mountaineers. Over the 7-day itinerary, you will embark on a 4-day trek from Kathmandu to Phakding via a Lukla flight, take a day trek to Namche, enjoy a day hike to Khumjung, and visit the Everest View Hotel to see more than eight of the highest mountains in the world. You will then trek back to Lukla to connect with your return flight to Kathmandu. In Kathmandu, you will have the chance to see hidden cultural monuments as well as enjoy city sightseeing.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#B22222"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Why Choose Us for a Luxury Everest Experience Trek?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Stay at a Top 5-Star Boutique Hotel:</strong> Enjoy the luxurious ambiance of Hotel Dwarika in Kathmandu.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Experience the Best Luxury Lodges:</strong> Relax in the comfort of Mountain lodges of Nepal(MLN), renowned for its exceptional hospitality.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Embark on a Short and Easy-Moderate Trek:</strong> Witness the breathtaking views of the highest peak in the world and other stunning mountains with a manageable trek.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Explore Diverse Cultures:</strong> Immerse yourself in the rich traditions of various ethnic groups in Nepal, including the Sherpas, famous for their mountaineering expertise.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#B22222"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Is This Trekking for Me? How Difficult is the Luxury Everest Experience Trek?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">The <strong>Luxury Everest Experience Trek</strong> is one of the shortest luxury treks in the Everest region, reaching a maximum altitude of 3,800 meters. This trek is categorized as easy to moderate, making it accessible for everyone.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">Previous trekking experience is not necessary, but you should be prepared to walk for 4&ndash;8 hours each day. Engaging in one hour of daily walking, running, or cycling can help you prepare for the trek. Participants of all age groups are welcome to join!</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:#B22222"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>The Best Season for the Luxury Everest view&nbsp;Trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">We recommend joining this trek during the optimal weather months, from mid-September to December or from March to mid-June. For the best photographic opportunities, consider trekking from mid-October to mid-December and from mid-March to mid-May.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="font-size:16px">However, this trek is possible year-round, as weather can be unpredictable; sometimes, the monsoon season can also offer clear skies.</span></p>	Luxury Everest Experience Trek - 7 Days Want to see Mount Everest in the shortest timeframe without a strenuous trek? Interested in an easy to moderate-level trek but worried about the quality of accommodation and food during the journey? What is the Luxury Everest view Trek and What Makes It Luxury? Our Luxury Everest Experience Trek addresses all your desires and requirements, fulfilling your thrill for a short and moderate trek at its best. This one-week trek in the Everest region invites you to spend nights in top-quality luxury lodges, such as mountain lodges of Nepal formerly known as Yeti Mountain Home, and enjoy a stay at a top 5-star hotel dwarika in Kathmandu. The Luxury Everest view Trek will guide you to the famous Everest View Hotel and the beautiful Khumjung Village above Namche, home to mountaineers. Over the 7-day itinerary, you will embark on a 4-day trek from Kathmandu to Phakding via a Lukla flight, take a day trek to Namche, enjoy a day hike to Khumjung, and visit the Everest View Hotel to see more than eight of the highest mountains in the world. You will then trek back to Lukla to connect with your return flight to Kathmandu. In Kathmandu, you will have the ch	<p><span style="color:#B22222"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Highlights of the Luxury Everest Experience Trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>The Easiest Trek to See Mount Everest:</strong> Experience breathtaking views of Mount Everest and over eight of Nepal&#39;s highest mountains.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Cultural Tour of Kathmandu:</strong> Explore the rich heritage and vibrant culture of Kathmandu city.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Panoramic Mountain Views:</strong> Enjoy a coffee break with stunning mountain vistas from the Everest View Hotel.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Finest Luxury Lodges:</strong> Stay in the best luxury lodges in the Everest region, ensuring comfort throughout your trek.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li>\r\n\t<p><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>Short Luxury Trek:</strong> Enjoy a memorable holiday with this short yet enriching Everest experience.</span></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n</ol>	<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif"><strong>Comfortable, deluxe accommodations and hygienic meals</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Luxury&nbsp;5-star (<span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>The Dwarika&#39;s Hotel)</strong></span></span>&nbsp;Hotel accommodation in Kathmandu on twin share with breakfast<span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>&nbsp;(2&nbsp;nights).</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">4 nights at a Luxury&nbsp;mountain lodge (<span style="font-size:18px"><span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><strong>&nbsp;Yeti Mountain Home- YMH)&nbsp;</strong></span><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>in PHAKDING( 1 night), NAMCHE( 2&nbsp;nights) &amp; LUKLA( 1 night)</strong></span></span><span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span>with an attached bathroom, including hot shower.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">There are 3 hygienic vegetarian or non-vegetarian meals per day: breakfast, lunch, and dinner (you can choose meals from all over the Lodge every day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tea/coffee or other hot beverages during breakfast, lunch, and dinner (5&ndash;6 cups per day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">seasonal fruits and additional biscuit/cookies snacks&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Wifi is available for free in the lodges.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">4-5 liters of free boiled or purified water</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Mobile/camera/laptop battery charges&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Private transportation that is comfortable</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">private, comfortable vehicle tour of Kathmandu city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">All airport transfers by private, comfortable vehicle (international and domestic airport pick-up and drop-off as included in the itinerary).</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>baggage allowance and domestic flights.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:14px">K<span style="font-size:16px">athmandu-Lukla-Kathmandu flight tickets</span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-size:16px">The baggage allowance on the Lukla flight is 15 kg, and we include 5 kg extra for free, for a total of 20 kg per person</span>.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Professional Private Expert Representatives &amp; porters</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">professional English-speaking tour guide for sightseeing in the city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A professional English-speaking guide for the trek</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Porter who is professional, dependable, helpful, and friendly (1 porter for every two people sharing)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Daily wage, lodging, meals, and guide and porter insurance.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Trekking permits and entrance fees</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Entrance fees to all UNESCO heritage sites during city sightseeing</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Everest National Park Fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The local government fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekker&rsquo;s information management system (TIMS) fee</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free information or guest services.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">guide to purchasing trekking clothing or equipment, as well as any other required wholesale shopping in Kathmandu.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support in the case of baggage loss or delay in Kathmandu from international flights to Nepal</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support to exchange money, get a local SIM card</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">24/7 emergency call support.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free safe baggage storage service during the trek</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free welcome dinner &amp; farewell 