="font-size:18px"><strong>What is the Deluxe Lobuche&nbsp;peak expedition &amp; what makes it Deluxe?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="498"><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>The Deluxe Lobuche Peak Expedition</strong>&nbsp;is another popular trekking peak climbing expedition in the Everest region of Nepal. The main goal of the Lobuche expedition is to fulfill your dream of climbing a peak and hiking at the base camp of the world&#39;s highest mountain, Mount Everest.Located at an altitude of 6119m, there are two Lobuche peaks&mdash;Lobuche east and Lobuche west. In this package, we are taking you to the summit of East Lobuche peak (6119m).</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="499"><span style="font-size:16px">Lobuche Peak Expedition is a moderate to difficult trekking and climbing expedition in the Khumbu valley that begins with a scenic mountain flight to Lukla, the starting point for the famous Gokyo Everest base camp trek, Everest High Pass Trek, and an expedition of over 90 high mountains in Sagarmatha National Park. Like other treks and climbs, Lobuche peak climbing follows the famous Tenzing Hillary trekking trail to Namche Bazaar from Lukla, with two days of first acclimatization on this trip, and the second acclimatization is at Pheriche, where you will hike to Nagarjun Hill (5000m) before heading toward hiking of Kala Patthar and Mount Everest base camp.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="500"><span style="font-size:16px">After successful trekking and hiking of EBC and Kala Patthar, you will trek toward Lobuche peak climbing. We will set up a night at high camp at approximately 5300m. The next morning, around 2 am, we start climbing Lobuche peak and return to high camp for another night, or we can move ahead to Pheriche or nearby. Compare to Island peak, this peak is easier to summit. After a successful summit of Lobuche peak, we will trek down to Lukla and fly back to Kathmandu.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="501"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Why should you book the Deluxe Lobuche&nbsp;peak expedition and Everest base camp&nbsp;trek with us?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="502"><span style="font-size:16px">During the entire expedition, NTT&nbsp;offers the best available&nbsp;<strong>deluxe lodges with attached bathrooms, hot showers,&nbsp;</strong>and hygienic Himalayan cuisine. With our more than 15 years of experience as Expert Representatives and porters, your dream trip of climbing Lobuche is possible with us. We also provide the best selected deluxe 3 star or 5 star hotels in Kathmandu and comfortable private vehicles as transportation during city tours and airport transfers. The Deluxe Lobuche Peak Expedition is a well-prepared itinerary for a safe, comfortable, and successful trip package for a journey of a lifetime.</span></div>\r\n\r\n<h4><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Is this trekking and climbing for me? How difficult is this expedition?</strong></span></span></h4>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="504"><span style="font-size:16px">Whenever you are interested in trekking and climbing peaks in Nepal, you have to think that it is a physically demanding trip which requires a minimum of 5&ndash;9 hours of trekking at an altitude of above 3000 to 6000m with the support of rope. Although the Lobuche peak expedition is not tough or technical, you should prepare well in advance for your physical fitness. Those who are prepared mentally and physically can accomplish their dream of reaching the top of the mountain.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<h4><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>The best season for the Deluxe Lobuche Peak Expedition:</strong></span></span></h4>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="506"><span style="font-size:16px">If you are an amateur photographer and would like to enjoy real scenery from the top of Lobuche peak or from the whole trip, you have to select the best months like October and November. Still, December is a fine month in early winter. The best spring months are April and May. If you want to trek at a less crowded time, we recommend joining us for this expedition in early September, at the end of monsoon season, or in June, at the start of monsoon season.</span></p>	Deluxe Lobuche Peak Expedition-17 days "The best peak climbing and trekking in Nepal's Everest National Park for an unforgettable once-in-a-lifetime experience." Deluxe Lobuche Peak Expedition Cost - 17-Day Full-Board Package Autumn Price (Mid-September to Mid-December): USD 2,599 per person. Spring Price (March to May): USD 2,777 per person. What is the Deluxe Lobuche peak expedition & what makes it Deluxe? The Deluxe Lobuche Peak Expedition is another popular trekking peak climbing expedition in the Everest region of Nepal. The main goal of the Lobuche expedition is to fulfill your dream of climbing a peak and hiking at the base camp of the world's highest mountain, Mount Everest.Located at an altitude of 6119m, there are two Lobuche peaks-Lobuche east and Lobuche west. In this package, we are taking you to the summit of East Lobuche peak (6119m). Lobuche Peak Expedition is a moderate to difficult trekking and climbing expedition in the Khumbu valley that begins with a scenic mountain flight to Lukla, the starting point for the famous Gokyo Everest base camp trek, Everest High Pass Trek, and an expedition of over 90 high mountains in Sagarmatha National Park. Like other treks and	<ol>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">The most popular trekking and climbing packages in Nepal with us</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">The Best Itinerary for Famous Trekking to Everest Base Camp + Kalapatthar Hike + Lobuche Peak Climbing.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">The ideal itinerary for safe acclimatization to ensure a 100% success rate in summiting Lobuche.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Comfortable accommodation that offers you a comfortable sleep in the mountains.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Cultural and historical tours of Kathmandu</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">The best 20 days of trekking and climbing holidays in Nepal with us</span></li>\r\n</ol>	<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif"><strong>Comfortable, deluxe accommodations and hygienic meals</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 4&nbsp;or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in Kathmandu on twin share with breakfast&nbsp;<span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>(2&nbsp;nights).</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>9 nights at a deluxe mountain lodge or guest house&nbsp;</strong></span>with an attached bathroom, including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>3 nights at the best selected lodge or guest house</strong></span>&nbsp;with a common bathroom including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>2 nights at Tented camp&nbsp;</strong></span>during climbing of Island peak</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">There are 3 hygienic vegetarian or non-vegetarian meals per day: breakfast, lunch, and dinner (you can choose meals from all over the Lodge every day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tea/coffee or other hot beverages during breakfast, lunch, and dinner (5&ndash;6 cups per day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">seasonal fruits and additional biscuit/cookies snacks&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Private transportation that is comfortable</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">private, comfortable vehicle tour of Kathmandu city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">All airport transfers by private, comfortable vehicle (international and domestic airport pick-up and drop-off as included in the itinerary).</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>baggage allowance and domestic flights.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><strong><span style="font-size:14px">K<span style="font-size:16px">athmandu-Lukla-Kathmandu flight tickets</span></span></strong></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-size:16px">The baggage allowance on the Lukla flight is 15 kg, and we include 5 kg extra for free, for a total of 20 kg per person</span>.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Professional Private Expert Representatives &amp; porters</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A professional English-speaking guide for the trek</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Porter who is professional, dependable, helpful, and friendly (1 porter for every two people sharing)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Daily wage, lodging, meals, and guide and porter insurance.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Professional Lobuche&nbsp;peak climbing Expert Representative, Insurance, climbing Bonus</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Extra porter for Lobuche&nbsp;peak&nbsp;climbing for foods, tents, sleeping gears</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Trekking permits,peak climbing permits&nbsp;and entrance fees</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Entrance fees to all UNESCO heritage sites during city sightseeing</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Everest National Park Fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The local government fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekker&rsquo;s information management system (TIMS) fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Lobuche peak climbing permit</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Lobuche peak Permit Garbage deposit Management</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free information or guest services.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">guide to purchasing trekking clothing or equipment, as well as any other required wholesale shopping in Kathmandu.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support in the case of baggage loss or delay in Kathmandu from international flights to Nepal</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support to exchange money, get a local SIM card</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">24/7 emergency call support.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free safe baggage storage service during the trek</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free welcome dinner &amp; farewell professional body massage after the trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">We offer a free welcome Nepalese dinner with authentic Nepalese cultural dances on arrival day, or if you arrive late on arrival night, this will be provided on the second day.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">After the trek, you will receive a FREE 1-hour Ayurvedic full-body massage as a treatment for your tired body.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Other free services include:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A down sleeping bag and a down jacket are provided at no cost.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of water bottles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of trekking poles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of porter duffel bags (you can take them after the trek if you like).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">First Aid Kit</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking &amp; Lobuche peak summited certificate</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking Map</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The company&#39;s gift</span></li>\r\n</ul>	<ul style="color: rgb(37, 37, 37);">\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Nepal Visa-US $ 50</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">International Flight to/from Kathmandu/home</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Travel and Emergency Helicopter Evacuation Insurance</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Meals (Lunch and Dinner) and other expenses while in Kathmandu (breakfast included at hotel)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Any soft drinks or alcoholic drinks during the trek, drinking water, battery charges, internet bills, dessert items, Except for breakfast, lunch, and dinner, extra tea/coffee or foods</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Laundry or personal expenses like internet WIFI, unforeseen costs due to natural disasters, sickness, flight delays, bad weat