mp( B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 12, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 12: Early morning 2 am after light breakfast, we start climbing Lobuche east peak, it takes nearly 6 hours to reach Top of Lobuche east peak( 6119 m), back to High camp-Tented camp( B+L+D)", "walking": "9-10 hours", "altitude": "5400 m", "distance": "12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Tented camp( B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 13, "meal": "Breakfast + lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 13: Extra day for bad weather or contingency day or Trek down to Pheriche/Pangboche( 4371m)>> 4/5 hours>> Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "walking": "4-5 hours Trekking", "altitude": "4371 m", "distance": "10 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 14, "meal": "Breakfast + lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 14: Trek down to Namche( 3440m)>> 5-6 hours>>  Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "walking": "5-6 hours trekking", "altitude": "3440 m", "distance": "11 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 15, "meal": "Breakfast + lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 15: Last day of Lobuche peak climbing trip: Trek down to Lukla( 2860 m)>> 7/8 hours>> 18 km>> Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "walking": "7-8 hours trekking", "altitude": "2860 m", "distance": "18 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe attached bathroom Lodge( B + L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 16, "meal": "Lavish Breakfast", "title": "Day 16: Lukla to Kathmandu flight( 35 minute), transfer to hotel, free day/relax day or shopping day- Deluxe Hotel( B+B)", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "1400 m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe Hotel( B+B)", "transportation": "35 min flight + Private car transfer to Hotel"}, {"day": 17, "meal": "Lavish breakfast", "title": "Day 17: Drive to TIA Airport in Kathmandu, Lobuche peak expedition holiday ends today.. departure to fly home.... see you again for another trip... B", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "1400 m", "distance": "8-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe Attached-Bath Lodge", "transportation": "Private car transfer to Airport"}]	[{"id": 243, "price": 2599, "status": 1, "endDate": "2026-11-29", "spotsLeft": 8, "startDate": "2026-11-13"}, {"id": 244, "price": 2599, "status": 1, "endDate": "2026-12-16", "spotsLeft": 6, "startDate": "2026-11-30"}]	[]	[{"id": 22, "date": "2022-07-26", "title": "Michael", "author": "Deluxe Lobuche Peak Expedition", "rating": 5, "comment": "Trip reviews of the Lobuche peak and Everest base camp trek Hello everyone. My name is Michael, and I am from Singapore. In March 2022, I made the trek to Everest Base Camp and climbed Lobuche Peak with two other friends. It wasn't easy to select the right company when you first planned to trek or climb a high mountain. We were finally convinced by Expert Representative's trek package after contacting more than five local companies. On arrival, Expert Representative himself welcomed us by sherpa cultural welcome in Kathmandu Airport with a white religious scarf (Khata). The hotel we booked was in the city, with all the facilities. The first welcome cultural dinner was so nice. Our Kathmandu city tour was very nice too, and we flew to Lukla for the Everest base camp hike. As promised and mentioned on the website, we are accommodated at upgraded deluxe lodges with attached bathrooms with hot showers in Namche, Lukla, Phakding and some other places above 4000m too. Even other lodges are best selected for their best values. Our guide, Lhakpa Sona, is a wonderful person who ensures that everything goes smoothly for us. We are given our own selected meals every day in each lodge. We trek toward Lobuche after visiting Everest Base Camp and Kala Patthar. We had another fantastic experience sleeping in a tent. We successfully summited Lobuche peak and returned to Kathmandu. Again, Expert Representative met us at Kathmandu Airport, took us to the hotel, and provided us with a free massage, which was another great experience for us. All in all, we had a very nice arrangement for our trekking holiday, which was truly a deluxe travel experience for us. We can't thank you enough for these wonderful vacation arrangements, and we would highly recommend booking any trips in Nepal with Expert Representative. We are looking forward to booking another trip again next time. Sincerely yours, MIchael, Singapore", "country": "singapore"}, {"id": 36, "date": "2024-11-20", "title": "Robert Gills", "author": "Wonderful EBC Trek with Lobuche peak climbing", "rating": 5, "comment": "Hello Expert Representative, I want to say thank you so much for making our Nepal trip excellent. The views from the top of Lobuche were marvelous, and we had a very professional climbing guide, Mingmar Sherpa. Your itinerary design worked so well-it was very comfortable, with great lodges and hotels. We had no issues and will definitely visit again with your company. We enjoyed everything you offered, and it was a very well-organized trip with the best services in Nepal. Thanks again!", "country": "Austria"}]	5.0	36	2026-10-23 20:31:04.764319+06
4	Deluxe Best of Annapurna Trek	deluxe-best-of-annapurna-trek	19 Days Guided Himalayan Adventure	deluxe-trekking	Annapurna	deluxe-nepal-trekking-tours	19	2155	2400	2255	2500	Moderate	5,416m (Thorong La) / 4,130m (ABC)	Spring (Mar-May) & Autumn (Sep-Nov)	4-Star City Hotel & Deluxe Attached-Bath Lodges	Full Board (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) on Trek	2 – 12 Guests (Private or Small Group)	f	bestseller	/images/upload/package/deluxe-best-of-annapurna-trek.jpg	["/images/upload/package/slider/deluxe-best-of-annapurna-trek.jpg"]	<p><strong><span style="font-size:22px">Deluxe Best of Annapurna Trek-19&nbsp;days</span> &gt; <span style="font-size:18px"><em>T</em></span></strong><span style="font-size:18px"><em>he best view A moderate-level&nbsp;trek inside Annapurna</em></span><strong> </strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><em><span style="font-size:16px">The Deluxe trek combines the four&nbsp;best Annapurna treks (<strong>Mardi Himal trek</strong>, <strong>Annapurna Base Camp trek</strong>, <strong>Ghorepani poonhill </strong>and <strong>Kobra Danda trek</strong>). </span></em></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="382"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>What is the Deluxe Base Camp Trek and what makes it Deluxe?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="true" data-paragraphid="366"><span style="font-size:16px"><strong>The Deluxe</strong><strong> Best of Annapurna Trek</strong>&nbsp;is one of the most precious trekking trails inside the Annapurna trekking region of Nepal. The 19-day long trek, including city tours of&nbsp;Pokhara, starts in one place and ends in another place. The best of Annapurna trek covers four of the most famous trekking trails in Annapurna in one trekking package-Mardi Himal trek, Annapurna base camp trek, Khopra ridge trek, and Ghorepani Poonhill trek.</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="true" data-paragraphid="367">&nbsp;</div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="368"><span style="font-size:16px">The beginning of the first week of this deluxe best of Annapurna trek starts from Khande to Australian Camp, which is the nearest trekking trail with the finest view of the Himalayas. The trail takes you to the highest point of the Mardi Himal trek, and then follows the trail to Deluxe Annapurna base camp.</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="true" data-paragraphid="369"><span style="font-size:16px">After the trek to Annapurna base camp, you will trek to the off-the-beaten-trail of Khopra ridge, also known as the Khayar Barah lake trek, and finally you will trek to Poonhill to see full panoramic views of the Himalayas. The whole trek offers the best mountain views, local culture, temples, and hot springs. From Ghorepani Poonhill trek, which is the last and best part of this trek, you will drive back to Pokhara city, which is the City of Paradise in Nepal.</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="true" data-paragraphid="371">&nbsp;</div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="372"><span style="font-size:16px">During the whole trekking period, you will stay at the best available lodges or guest houses, enjoying the best hygienic cuisine, and that&rsquo;s why the trek is known as the &quot;deluxe Annapurna trek.&quot; The highest points of this trek are Mardi Himal base camp and Annapurna base camp, which are less than 4500m. This trek required good physical fitness as well as daily hiking or trekking experience, mostly up and down.</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="true" data-paragraphid="373">&nbsp;</div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="374"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Why should you book a Deluxe Best of Annapurna Trek with us?</strong></span></span></div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="375"><span style="font-size:16px">The Best of Annapurna Deluxe Trek is the only trek package available with us in Nepal. This is a well designed itinerary that lets you explore the pure beauty of the Annapurna Sanctuary. During the whole trek, you will be welcomed by the best available lodges or deluxe attached bathroom lodges where available. You will be guided by some of the most expert local Expert Representatives as well as facilitated by sherpa porters. The most important reason to book this trek with us is our personalized deluxe service of accommodation, flights, transport, and quality service that makes sure you have a trip of a lifetime.</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="383">&nbsp;</div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="376"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Is this trek for me? How difficult is this trek?</strong></span></span></div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="377"><span style="font-size:16px">This trek does not involve any high passes or the longest walk. To enjoy this trek most, one should be physically fit to trek 5-7 hours a day with lots of breaks to enjoy the views of the Himalayas and take photos. The itinerary is well prepared to minimize the risk of altitude sickness. This trek is suitable for all aged trekkers who wish to enjoy the grand scenery of the full beauty of four popular Annapurna treks in one package.</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="true" data-paragraphid="378">&nbsp;</div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="379"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>The best season for Deluxe&#39;s best of Annapurna Trek:</strong></span></span></div>\r\n\r\n<div class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="380"><span style="font-size:16px">The best months for this trek are mid-September to mid-December and March to May in the spring season. However, if you wish to trek in blue sky clear weather, it is recommended to trek from mid-October to November or up to mid-December. In spring, it is best to trek from mid-March to mid-May. Other months are also okay too.</span></div>	Deluxe Best of Annapurna Trek-19 days &gt; T he best view A moderate-level trek inside Annapurna The Deluxe trek combines the four best Annapurna treks ( Mardi Himal trek , Annapurna Base Camp trek , Ghorepani poonhill and Kobra Danda trek ). What is the Deluxe Base Camp Trek and what makes it Deluxe? The Deluxe Best of Annapurna Trek is one of the most precious trekking trails inside the Annapurna trekking region of Nepal. The 19-day long trek, including city tours of Pokhara, starts in one place and ends in another place. The best of Annapurna trek covers four of the most famous trekking trails in Annapurna in one trekking package-Mardi Himal trek, Annapurna base camp trek, Khopra ridge trek, and Ghorepani Poonhill trek. The beginning of the first week of this deluxe best of Annapurna trek starts from Khande to Australian Camp, which is the nearest trekking trail with the finest view of the Himalayas. The trail takes you to the highest point of the Mardi Himal trek, and then follows the trail to Deluxe Annapurna base camp. After the trek to Annapurna base camp, you will trek to the off-the-beaten-trail of Khopra ridge, also known as the Khayar Barah lake trek, and finally you wil	<ol>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Truely the best of Annapurna:</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Mardi Himal, Annapurna base camp, Khopra Ridge/Khayar Lake trek, Ghorepani Poonhill trek-four<strong>&nbsp;treks combined</strong></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Cultural</strong> tours in&nbsp;Pokhara</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Enjoy the moderate level trek to enjoy the best views during the whole trek.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">The Best Deal on Deluxe Service Trek because of the best designed itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Domestic flights are included for the Kathmandu-Pokhara sector to make this a deluxe experience.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Trek with local expert Expert Representatives and porters.</span></li>\r\n</ol>	<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif"><strong>Comfortable, deluxe accommodations and hygienic meals</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 4&nbsp;or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in&nbsp;<span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>KATHMANDU&nbsp;o</strong></span>n twin share with breakfast&nbsp;<span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)">(<strong>2&nbsp;nights)</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 4&nbsp;or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in&nbsp;<span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>POKHARA</strong></span>&nbsp;on twin share with breakfast&nbsp;<span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)">(1<strong>&nbsp;nights)</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:rgb(128, 0, 0)"><strong>3 nights at a deluxe mountain lodge&nbsp;</strong></span>or guest house with an attached bathroom, including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>12 nights at the best selected lodge</strong></span>&nbsp;or guest house with a common bathroom including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">There are 3 hygienic vegetarian or non-vegetarian meals per day: breakfast, lunch, and dinner (you can choose meals from all over the Lodge every day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tea/coffee or other hot beverages during breakfast, lunch, and dinner (5&ndash;6 cups per day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">seasonal fruits and additional biscuit/cookies snacks&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Private transportation that is comfortable</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">private, comfortable vehicle tour of Kathmandu city &amp; Pokhara City&nbsp;as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">All airport transfers by private, comfortable vehicle (international and domestic airport pick-up and drop-off as included in the itinerary).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><strong>Pokhara- Pherdi &amp; Ulleri- Pokhara by Private Jee</strong></span>p( before/after trek)</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>baggage allowance and domestic flights.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="color:#8B4513"><strong><span style="font-size:14px">K<span style="font-size:16px">athmandu-Pokhara-Kathmandu flight tickets</span></span></strong></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-size:16px">The baggage allowance on the Pokhara&nbsp;flight is 15 kg, and we include 5 kg extra for free, for a total of 20 kg per person</span>.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Professional Private Expert Representatives &amp; porters</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">professional English-speaking tour guide for sightseeing in the city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A professional English-speaking guide for the trek</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Porter who is professional, dependable, helpful, and friendly (1 porter for every two people sharing)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Daily wage, lodging, meals, and guide and porter insurance.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Trekking permits and entrance fees</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Entrance fees to all UNESCO heritage sites during city sightseeing in Pokhara</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Annapurna conservation Area Project( ACAP)&nbsp;Entrance&nbsp;Fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The local government fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekker&rsquo;s information management system (TIMS) fee</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free information or guest services.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">guide to purchasing trekking clothing or equipment, as well as any other required wholesale shopping in Kathmandu.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support in the case of baggage loss or delay in Kathmandu from international flights to Nepal</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support to exchange money, get a local SIM card</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">24/7 emergency call support.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free safe baggage storage service during the trek</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free welcome dinner &amp; farewell professional body massage after the trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">We offer a free welcome Nepalese dinner with authentic Nepalese cultural dances on arrival day, or if you arrive late on arrival night, this will be provided on the second day.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">After the trek, you will receive a FREE 1-hour Ayurvedic full-body massage as a treatment for your tired body.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Other free services include:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A down sleeping bag and a down jacket are provided at no cost.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of water bottles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of trekking poles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of porter duffel bags (you can take them after the trek if you like).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">First Aid Kit</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking certificate</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking Map</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The company&#39;s gift</span></li>\r\n</ul>	<ul>\r\n\t<li>Nepal Visa- US$ 30</li>\r\n\t<li>International Flight to/from Kathmandu/home</li>\r\n\t<li>Travel and Emergency Helicopter Evacuation Insurance</li>\r\n\t<li>Meals (Lunch &amp; Dinner) &amp; other expenses during Kathmandu &amp; Pokhara (breakfast included at Hotel)</li>\r\n\t<li>Any soft drinks or Alcoholic drinks during trek, drinking water, Battery charges,&nbsp;internet bills,deserts items, Extra tea/coffee or foods except Breakfast, Lunch &amp; Dinner time</li>\r\n\t<li>Laundry or personal expenses like internet WIFI, unforeseen cost due to Natural disaster, sick, flight delayed, bad weather, Urgent Helicopter Evacuation etc</li>\r\n\t<li>Trekking gears and clothing</li>\r\n\t<li>Tips for guide and porter</li>\r\n</ul>		[{"label": "1 Traveler (Solo Private)", "maxPax": 1, "minPax": 1, "deluxePrice": 2405, "luxuryPrice": 2605}, {"