nd Pokhara were also excellent.Our guide and porter took great care of us throughout the trek, ensuring everything went smoothly. A big thank you to Expert Representative and the team for providing such an excellent trekking experience. We look forward to seeing you again soon!", "country": "australia"}]	5.0	16	2026-10-23 20:31:04.764319+06
16	Deluxe Upper Mustang Trek	deluxe-upper-mustang-trek	17 Days Guided Himalayan Adventure	deluxe-trekking	Mustang	deluxe-nepal-trekking-tours	17	2599	3000	2799	3250	Moderate	4,500m	Spring (Mar-May) & Autumn (Sep-Nov)	4-Star City Hotel & Deluxe Attached-Bath Lodges	Full Board (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) on Trek	2 – 12 Guests (Private or Small Group)	f	bestseller	/images/upload/package/new-project-23.jpg	["/images/upload/package/new-project-23.jpg", "/images/unsplash/photo-1518002054494-3a6f94352e9d-1200.jpg", "/images/unsplash/photo-1464822759023-fed622ff2c3b-1200.jpg"]	<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="428"><span style="font-size:22px"><strong>Deluxe Upper Mustang Trek -17</strong> days</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="429"><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe Upper Mustang trek,&nbsp;typically known as the &quot;rain shadow&quot; trekking region of the Mustang district in Nepal. Jomsom is the headquarters as well as the only airport in the Mustang district, which is the gateway to the Lower and Upper Mustang regions. During the 17-day&nbsp;upper Mustang trek, you will have experience of the best available lodges and guest houses. Until 1992, upper Mustang hiking was restricted to districts and still dominated by its own local king. There are many Tibetan inhabitants in Mustang, and many people speak both Tibetan and Nepali. The main highlights of this trek are the centuries-old monasteries, its magnificent geographical attractions, unique chortens and houses, typical local people and their cultures, and the mountains.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="430"><span style="font-size:16px">The mustang region is located above the tree-lined and desert regions, with a dry climate even during the monsoon season (July-September).When other trekking regions attract heavy rain, the Mustang district receives less rain in summer or monsoon months. That&rsquo;s why it is normally possible to hike in Mustang in the summer too.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="431"><span style="font-size:16px">Muktinath Temple: One of the most holy temples, known as the Temple of Vishnu, is sacred to both Hindus and Buddhists. Lo-manthang was the walled capital of the Mustang district and is now a rural municipality. During this deluxe upper Mustang trek, you will trek up to the Lo-manthang and return the same way to Jomsom. Kagbeni is the main entrance to Upper Mustang, a trek with a special hiking permit of a minimum of 10 days or more with a fixed itinerary to enter this forbidden kingdom.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="432"><span style="font-size:16px">From Pokhara, you will fly to Jomsom to start the trek and fly back to Pokhara after the trek. However, driving to Jomsom is another&nbsp;option if a flight is canceled due to the weather. Optionally, you can do a side trek from Tatopani to Ghorepani.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="434"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>What is the deluxe upper Mustang trek? Why do you join this trek with us?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="435"><span style="font-size:16px">The Deluxe Upper Mustang Trek is an upgraded trek package for high-quality trekking service that includes the best lodge accommodation, the best hygienic meals, and four domestic flights from Kathmandu to Pokhara to Jomsom and back. All of the hotels in Kathmandu and Pokhara are three or five stars, depending on the package you book with us. In order to get the best quality service at the best price, you have to book this trek with us.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="437"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Is this trekking for me? How difficult is the Deluxe Upper Mustang Trek?</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="438"><span style="font-size:16px">The highest altitude of this trek is less than 4000m. It is a moderate-level trek. Previous trekking experience is not really necessary. However, it will support your physical fitness. It is recommended to start exercising in preparation.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="440"><span style="color:#A52A2A"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>The best season for the Deluxe Upper Mustang Trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class="root-block-node" data-changed="false" data-paragraphid="441"><span style="font-size:16px">Since upper Mustang trekking lies in the rain shadow area, it does not rain heavily in the monsoon or summer season. That&rsquo;s why you can do this trek in the summer months (July-September) too. However, the best months to do this trek are September to November and March to May.</span></p>\r\n	Deluxe Upper Mustang Trek -17 days Deluxe Upper Mustang trek, typically known as the "rain shadow" trekking region of the Mustang district in Nepal. Jomsom is the headquarters as well as the only airport in the Mustang district, which is the gateway to the Lower and Upper Mustang regions. During the 17-day upper Mustang trek, you will have experience of the best available lodges and guest houses. Until 1992, upper Mustang hiking was restricted to districts and still dominated by its own local king. There are many Tibetan inhabitants in Mustang, and many people speak both Tibetan and Nepali. The main highlights of this trek are the centuries-old monasteries, its magnificent geographical attractions, unique chortens and houses, typical local people and their cultures, and the mountains. The mustang region is located above the tree-lined and desert regions, with a dry climate even during the monsoon season (July-September).When other trekking regions attract heavy rain, the Mustang district receives less rain in summer or monsoon months. That's why it is normally possible to hike in Mustang in the summer too. Muktinath Temple: One of the most holy temples, known as the Temple of Vishn	<ol>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">The best upper Mustang trekking package at the best price.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">The best itinerary for acclimatization and to see all the nicest things</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Deluxe lodges with daily hot showers and hygienic meals</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Four internal flights: Kathmandu-Pokhara-Jomsom-Pokhara-Kathmandu.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">A well prepared itinerary covering all the important monasteries, caves, and monuments is included in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">A religious visit to Muktinath temple</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Pokhara city tour</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:18px">Tour of four UNESCO World Heritage Sites in Kathmandu&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n	<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><span style="font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif"><strong>Comfortable, deluxe accommodations and hygienic meals</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 3 or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in&nbsp;<span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>KATHMANDU</strong>&nbsp;</span>on twin share with breakfast <span style="color:#800000"><strong>(2&nbsp;nights)</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Deluxe 3 or 5-star (depending on the package) Hotel accommodation in&nbsp;<span style="color:#8B4513"><strong>POKHARA</strong></span>&nbsp;on twin share with breakfast <span style="color:#800000"><strong>(2&nbsp;nights)</strong></span></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><strong><span style="color:#8B4513">3 nights at a deluxe mountain lodge</span>&nbsp;</strong>or guest house with an attached bathroom, including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px"><strong><span style="color:#8B4513">9 nights at the best selected lodge</span>&nbsp;</strong>or guest house with a common bathroom including hot and cold showers.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">There are 3 hygienic vegetarian or non-vegetarian meals per day: breakfast, lunch, and dinner (you can choose meals from all over the Lodge every day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tea/coffee or other hot beverages during breakfast, lunch, and dinner (5&ndash;6 cups per day).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">seasonal fruits and additional biscuit/cookies snacks&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Private transportation that is comfortable</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">private, comfortable vehicle tour of Kathmandu city &amp; Pokhara City&nbsp;as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">All airport transfers by private, comfortable vehicle (international and domestic airport pick-up and drop-off as included in the itinerary).</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>baggage allowance and domestic flights.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="color:#8B4513"><strong><span style="font-size:14px">K<span style="font-size:16px">athmandu-Pokhara-Kathmandu flight tickets</span></span></strong></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="color:#8B4513"><strong><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-size:16px">Pokhara- Jomsom- Pokhara flights</span></span></strong></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:14px"><span style="font-size:16px">The baggage allowance on the Pokhara&nbsp;flight is 15 kg, and we include 5 kg extra for free, for a total of 20 kg per person</span>.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Professional Private Expert Representatives &amp; porters</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">professional English-speaking tour guide for sightseeing in the city as specified in the itinerary.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A professional English-speaking guide for the trek</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Porter who is professional, dependable, helpful, and friendly (1 porter for every two people sharing)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Daily wage, lodging, meals, and guide and porter insurance.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Trekking permits and entrance fees</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Entrance fees to all UNESCO heritage sites during city sightseeing in Kathmandu and Pokhara</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Annapurna conservation Area Project( ACAP)&nbsp;Entrance&nbsp;Fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="color:#A52A2A"><strong><span style="font-size:16px">Mustang restricted area special permit for 10 days (US$ 500) per person</span></strong></span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The local government fee</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekker&rsquo;s information management system (TIMS) fee</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free information or guest services.</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">guide to purchasing trekking clothing or equipment, as well as any other required wholesale shopping in Kathmandu.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support in the case of baggage loss or delay in Kathmandu from international flights to Nepal</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Support to exchange money, get a local SIM card</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">24/7 emergency call support.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free safe baggage storage service during the trek</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Free welcome dinner &amp; farewell professional body massage after the trek</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">We offer a free welcome Nepalese dinner with authentic Nepalese cultural dances on arrival day, or if you arrive late on arrival night, this will be provided on the second day.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">After the trek, you will receive a FREE 1-hour Ayurvedic full-body massage as a treatment for your tired body.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style="color:rgb(139, 69, 19)"><span style="font-size:18px"><strong>Other free services include:</strong></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">A down sleeping bag and a down jacket are provided at no cost.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of water bottles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of trekking poles</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Free use of porter duffel bags (you can take them after the trek if you like).</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">First Aid Kit</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking certificate</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking Map</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">The company&#39;s gift</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n	<ul style="color: rgb(37, 37, 37);">\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Nepal Visa-US $ 50</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">International Flight to/from Kathmandu/home</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Travel and Emergency Helicopter Evacuation Insurance</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Meals (Lunch and Dinner) and other expenses while in Kathmandu (breakfast included at hotel)</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Any soft drinks or alcoholic drinks during the trek, drinking water, battery charges, internet bills, dessert items, Except for breakfast, lunch, and dinner, extra tea/coffee or foods</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Laundry or personal expenses like internet WIFI, unforeseen costs due to natural disasters, sickness, flight delays, bad weather, urgent helicopter evacuation etc.</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Trekking gear and clothing</span></li>\r\n\t<li><span style="font-size:16px">Tips for guides and porters</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n		[{"label": "1 Traveler (Solo Private)", "maxPax": 1, "minPax": 1, "deluxePrice": 2849, "luxuryPrice": 3149}, {"label": "2 – 3 Travelers", "maxPax": 3, "minPax": 2, "deluxePrice": 2599, "luxuryPrice": 2799}, {"label": "4 – 6 Travelers", "maxPax": 6, "minPax": 4, "deluxePrice": 2417, "luxuryPrice": 2603}, {"label": "7 – 12 Travelers (Group)", "maxPax": 12, "minPax": 7, "deluxePrice": 2261, "luxuryPrice": 2435}]	[{"day": 1, "meal": "FREE welcome cultural Dinner", "title": "Day 01. Arrival in Nepal and warm welcome for best deluxe upper mustang trek, meet/greet in Airport, transfer to hotel, relax day and evening join welcome cultural dinner-Deluxe Hotel( D)", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "1400 m", "distance": "8-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe Hotel( D)", "transportation": "Private Car transfer to Hotel"}, {"day": 2, "meal": " Lavish Breakfast", "title": "Day 02. Morning breakfast meeting for permit and trek preparation.Then you will proceed for city tour of Kathmandu, total 2 UNESCO world heritage sites tour ( 3-4hours), afternoon fly to Pokhara( 25 min), transfer to hotel>> Deluxe Hotel( B+B))", "walking": "-", "altitude": "822 m", "distance": "35-40 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe Hotel( B+B))", "transportation": "Private Car tour- 7/8 hours tour in Kathmandu"}, {"day": 3, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner( B+L+D)", "title": "Day 03: Early morning drive to Airport with packed breakfast, first scenic 25 mountain flight to Jomsom(2720m) & short tea break, Trek to Kagbeni (2810m)>>11 km>>4 hours>>Deluxe Lodge with attached bathroom (B+L+D)", "walking": "4-5 hours Trekking", "altitude": "2810 m", "distance": "11 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe Lodge with attached bathroom (B+L+D)", "transportation": "25 min flight + 4 hours trekking"}, {"day": 4, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 04: Breakfast and enjoy mountains today.Today we trek from Kagbeni Trek to Chele( 3100m)>>15.3 km>> 6-7 hrs->>Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "walking": "6-7 hours trekking", "altitude": "3100m", "distance": "15.3 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 5, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 05: Have healthy breakfast and Trek from Chele to Syangmochen (3800m)>> 11.5 km >>6 hrs>> Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "walking": "6-7 hours Trekking", "altitude": "3800 m", "distance": "11.5 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 6, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 06:    Trek to Ghami (3510m) - Dhakmar (3820m)>>13.3 km >> 6 hrs>>Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "walking": "6-7 hour Trekking", "altitude": "3820 m", "distance": "13.3 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 7, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 07: Today we visit Ghar Gomba (3950m ), the oldest monastery and continue trek to - Lo- Manthang (3840m )>>17.2 km>> 7/8 hrs>>Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "walking": "7-8 hours trekking", "altitude": "3840 m", "distance": "17.2 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 8, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 08:  Another free day at Lo-manthang for exploration.. today we visit 3 important monasteries of Lo-manthang( 3840m) >> 2-3 hrs>> Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "walking": "2 hours walking tours", "altitude": "3840m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 9, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 09: Today after breakfast we will hike to Chosar Valley or optional Horse ride( extra cost) to explore monasteries & Jhong Cave>>6/7 hrs>> Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "walking": "6-7 hours trekking", "altitude": "3840m", "distance": "12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 10, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 10: from Today we are concluding trek of Upper mustang, today we Trek back to Charang (3570m)>>11 km>>5/6 hrs>>Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "walking": "5-6 hours Trekking", "altitude": "3570 m", "distance": "11 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 11, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 11:Today we return Trek to Syangbochen( 3800m)>> 13 km>> 6/7 hrs- Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "walking": "6-7 hours Trekking", "altitude": "3800 m", "distance": "13 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 12, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 12:  after breakfast We continue Trek return to Chhusang(3050m)>> 15 km >>6/7 hrs-Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "walking": "5-6 hours Trekking", "altitude": "3050 m", "distance": "15 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Lodge with hot shower (B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 13, "meal": "Breakfast + Lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 13: After breakfast, we continue Trek return back to Kagbeni( 2810m)>> 10 km >>5-6 hrs- Deluxe Lodge with attached bathroom( B+L+D)", "walking": "5-6 hours trekking", "altitude": "2810m", "distance": "10 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe Lodge with attached bathroom( B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 14, "meal": "Breakfast + lunch + Dinner(B+L+D)", "title": "Day 14: After breakfast, We hike to Muktinath temple and continue Trek to Jomsom( 2720m)>> 15 km>> 6/7 hours- Deluxe Lodge with attached bathroom( B+L+D)", "walking": "6-7 hours trekking", "altitude": "2720 m", "distance": "15 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe Lodge with attached bathroom( B+L+D)", "transportation": "On Foot / Trekking"}, {"day": 15, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Day 15: Mustang trek ended here! First flight back to Pokhara( 822m), check in Hotel & Half day tour in Pokhara( 3 hrs), rest day free to explore the city- Deluxe Hotel( B+B)", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "822 m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe Hotel( B+B)", "transportation": "25 min flight + 3/4 hours tour in Pokhara"}, {"day": 16, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Day 16:  After healthy morning breakfast, Flight back to Kathmandu, check in hotel, Half day tour in Kathmandu- Deluxe Hotel( B+B)", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "1400m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "Deluxe Hotel( B+B)", "transportation": "25 min flight + 3/4 hours tour in Kathmandu"}, {"day": 17, "meal": "Breakfast", "title": "Day 17. final shopping day until your flight to Kathmandu Airport, deluxe mustang trek concluded. see you again... B", "walking": "5-6 hours", "altitude": "1400 m", "distance": "10-12 km", "description": "Full guided day in the Himalayas with luxury lodge hospitality and scenic trails.", "accommodation": "-", "transportation": "Private car transfer to Airport"}]	[{"id": 151, "price": 2599, "status": "Guaranteed", "endDate": "2026-11-15", "spotsLeft": 6, "startDate": "2026-11-01"}, {"id": 152, "price": 2599, "status": "Available", "endDate": "2026-11-29", "spotsLeft": 8, "startDate": "2026-11-15"}, {"id": 153, "price": 2599, "status": 